{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars","id":1191798,"title":"Sell Me On: Feeling Strongly About Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-04T18:55:46-08:00","id":1191798,"title":"Sell Me On: Feeling Strongly About Lunars","content":"I really don't understand what about Lunars is such a point of contention for people. I've always seen them as... fine. They're OK. They're not my favorite Exalted. I don't hate them. They're just fine. I get the role they serve, I can come up with some character concepts for them, I think they have some neat aesthetics and themes.<br /> <br /> But why do people feel so strongly about them? What are they arguing about? How is &quot;Meerkat Steals The Spotlight Prana&quot; a thing?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:24:32-08:00","id":1191809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars#post1191798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But why do people feel so strongly about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI'd say that the heart of all arguments is that being an area that has generally been seen to not live up to its potential, and unclear or conflicting ideas about how that might be improved upon, creates a space in which that kind of impassioned argument can develop. In a sense, that there is something <i>to</i> argue about, in a way that most other parts of the setting and system are decided enough to lack.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and a few aspects of their premise made them a place to accumulate every new idea somebody had about something that should be in the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:30:49-08:00","id":1191810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1191809#post1191809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI'd say that the heart of all arguments is that being an area that has generally been seen to not live up to its potential, and unclear or conflicting ideas about how that might be improved upon, creates a space in which that kind of impassioned argument can develop. In a sense, that there is something <i>to</i> argue about, in a way that most other parts of the setting and system are decided enough to lack.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat and a few aspects of their premise made them a place to accumulate every new idea somebody had about something that should be in the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting. Please elaborate. How are these arguments divided? How do people want to see Lunars realized?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:36:19-08:00","id":1191811,"title":"","content":"Lunars have a lot of potential to be really cool and interesting. Unfortunately they have utterly failed to live up to that potential. For many people the idea of Lunars in their heads, the Lunars who have reached their potential, are awesome and they're unhappy about where Lunars currently stand (or stood) in the gameline. Unfortunately the awesome Lunar Exalted in my head are probably different from the awesome Lunar Exalted that are in someone else's head, and the things I think need to be done to make Lunars live up to their potential are things someone else might feel would completely ruin them. So even among Lunar fans there's often a lot of disagreement over what exactly is wrong with them and what needs to be done to make them better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:37:59-08:00","id":1191812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1191811#post1191811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars have a lot of potential to be really cool and interesting. Unfortunately they have utterly failed to live up to that potential. For many people the idea of Lunars in their heads, the Lunars who have reached their potential, are awesome and they're unhappy about where Lunars currently stand (or stood) in the gameline. Unfortunately the awesome Lunar Exalted in my head are probably different from the awesome Lunar Exalted that are in someone else's head, and the things I think need to be done to make Lunars live up to their potential are things someone else might feel would completely ruin them. So even among Lunar fans there's often a lot of disagreement over what exactly is wrong with them and what needs to be done to make them better.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather like to hear the opinions of the major camps. What are the ideas of how to portray Lunars that are so diametrically opposed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:55:51-08:00","id":1191816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1191810#post1191810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Please elaborate. How are these arguments divided? How do people want to see Lunars realized?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat... is a complicated subject involving more than a decade of arguments and many positions that mix and match numerous points. It's difficult to elaborate on, or even summarise effectively.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe best that I can come up with is a list of some of the more noteworthy contentious points. (And by noteworthy, I mean things that I can manage to remember)<br /> <br /> There are:<br /> <br /> \u200b* people who dislike Heart's Blood shapeshifting, either wanting a more freeform kind ala characters such as Mystique, or just a method of acquiring forms besides hunting and killing (or for it to take front and centre).<br /> * people who dislike the animal association.<br /> \u200b* people who dislike the Solar association.<br /> \u200b* people who think that a conflict with the Realm is nonsensical.<br /> \u200b* people who think that the setting should be filled with the results of Lunar nation building, crowding out the Realm.<br /> * people who think they should be reigning princes of the Wyld, drawn back to Creation solely by the return of the Solars.<br /> \u200b* people who want the shapeshifting to lean more towards the fantastical or alien.<br /> * people who primarily want to focus on them as a kind of mirror Exalted.<br /> \u200b* people who want them to have established princedoms throughout all of the realms of existence, and have a primary schtick about moving between them.<br /> \u200b* people who were really on board with the Thousand Streams River.<br /> \u200b* people who wanted chimerism to be viable as a transhumanist path to ultimate power.<br /> <br /> And many more.<br /> <br /> I think you get the gist of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T19:59:18-08:00","id":1191817,"title":"","content":"Right. Sorry if I'm forcing you to simplify a complex subject. It's just an aspect of the fandom that I never really understood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T20:13:33-08:00","id":1191822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1191810#post1191810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting. Please elaborate. How are these arguments divided? How do people want to see Lunars realized?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, on at least one count, people saw them as general shapeshifters. This tended to be encouraged by second edition, which abandoned any notion of first edition out of an extreme knee-jerk reaction. It was somewhat understandable, but still left everything hanging because of a poor execution. Poor execution is, ultimately, a bad reason to walk back from the concept of &quot;bestial shapeshifters that freak out most people who aren't living on the edge&quot;, because that premise is quite rich with possibilities. You can't let yourself get bogged down by Charm Bushes or a quizzical inclusion of the concept of Renown; these things are not central to kindle that theme.<br /> <br /> And the concept of bestial shapeshifters itself for whatever reason tends people to vastly underestimate where they should stand. They're not tiny obstacles to be swept aside. They are existential threats wearing the skins of beasts. Turning into an animal is something that people scoff at, but Lunar Exalted are of such puissance that when they do it, it utterly overpowers the might of dragons and slips around the foresight of the stars. They tackle the power of demons, throw down their adversaries, and smite them with the features of beasts. But no one did this, twice in a row, even though it seems like it would be a gimme for a company that made arguably the most powerful werewolves and other werebeasts around in the rpg industry.<br /> <br /> Further, there are people who disagree that the above is what they are. I recall much acrimony over this point, basically exploding on the forums six years ago after the final errata hit but long before the plans for EX3 were public knowledge. There was much bemoaning apparently not being able play Mystique from some parties, because they would have to choose a spirit shape and turn into animals as well as humans. There was a persistent cry to be like T-1000. Nowadays, we have other Exalted slated to act as shapeshifters, so those hats can go elsewhere, but in those days, the thinking was locked into the Exalted from 2e alone fulfilling every last archetype there was, which meant that Lunars were being stretched to be some kind of omni-shapeshifter, and people had it in their heads that it would be way better and more impressive if they relegated and/or cut turning into animals in some fashion.<br /> <br /> Except that Lunars are still based on W:tA and have a lot in common with its themes and fixtures, They had, and have always had, a focus, even if some of the writing tried to run away from it twice over. That reference to the &quot;unfinished&quot; world in EX3 likely means unfinished as in raw, rough, and naked. It's not much of a journey from there, if any at all, to being wild and untamed. I do tend to lean on the shapeshifting into animals and other humans part, but this plays into another similarity to W:tA, wherein the focus is on the world, as it exists through a bedrock of primal spirits. Between that and Luna's affection for Gaia living in her Exalted, I'd guess that Lunars are also meant to have bloody or unrestrained ritual practices that grant benefits that are normally had through more pedestrian (and predictable, traceable) means. We already have one standing example in ecstatic visions and trances across some of their earlier Charms, not just in terms of telling the future, but also the hacking methods that they got in the Modern Era shard.<br /> <br /> The further answer to your question probably lies more in responses to this post than in the post itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-04T22:26:45-08:00","id":1191843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1191822#post1191822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the concept of bestial shapeshifters itself for whatever reason tends people to vastly underestimate where they should stand. They're not tiny obstacles to be swept aside. They are existential threats wearing the skins of beasts. Turning into an animal is something that people scoff at, but Lunar Exalted are of such puissance that when they do it, it utterly overpowers the might of dragons and slips around the foresight of the stars. They tackle the power of demons, throw down their adversaries, and smite them with the features of beasts. But no one did this, twice in a row, even though it seems like it would be a gimme for a company that made arguably the most powerful werewolves and other werebeasts around in the rpg industry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that's where the mechanics blew the idea up. Generally speaking a Lunar Exalt, wielding an artifact weapon, was stronger than any form he could turn into (barring a few niche examples like Tyrant Lizards). This was compounded by Form Lock, where a Lunar essentially couldn't spend much Essence while in an animal form to increase their combat capability, save for the animal form that counted as one of their &quot;true forms&quot;. Sure your Lunar could turn into a bear and fight, but you'd probably be better off not bothering, and even if you did, within a couple of rounds you probably wouldn't be able to stay in your bear form anymore anyway. <br /> <br /> Coupled with this was the fact that Lunars could turn into animals for free at character creation, whereas if they wanted to turn into other stuff, they had to buy Charms to upgrade their transformation powers. As a result animal shifting was largely viewed as the basic, introductory power and many people thought about Lunars in terms of turning into other things. To a large degree the mechanics encouraged players to think about this. <br /> <br /> This tended to mean that when it came to shapeshifting, turning into animals outside of spying on someone or travelling quickly was fairly pointless and many of the more useful shapeshifting effects were things players had to spend experience on. That's how things were for two editions (about 15 years) and why many people tend to pooh pooh the idea of turning into animals, since it was generally wasn't as impressive as you might think for the vast majority of the game's existence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T00:54:34-08:00","id":1191861,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s worth noting that, when 1e was being developed, apparently the Lunars were going to be the hunting hounds of the Fae, exalted that had been corrupted by the wyld into insane servants. Deciding that they were going to be playable was apparently an 11th hour decision, which meant that they weren\u2019t really included in history or in the setting. They felt like an afterthought because they were. <br /> <br /> Heck, the Alchemical Exalted were apparently figured out conceptually before that, so they actually fit into the setting better than Lunars in 1e. <br /> <br /> So, that helped contribute to the mess they had to deal with in both previous editions and to the perception that the 2e Lunar charmset is broken and the Sidereal one fine (the Lunar one works, but it\u2019s kinda boring and a thematic mess, while the Sids charmset is pretty cool thematically, but, because they copied so much directly from 1e, it doesn\u2019t interact properly with the rest of the game in many important ways).<br /> <br /> So, yes, there\u2019s always been lots to talk about in regards to Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T05:42:33-08:00","id":1191899,"title":"","content":"Going way, way back, Werewolf was the first game where you could play a distinctly &quot;monstrous&quot; character without being a cardboard cutout villain. <br /> <br /> Vampire also had traditionally antagonistic characters presented as player characters, but vamps look and act like humans, and assume that their supernatural coolness factor is a curse. Mage had otherwise-regular people who could do Magick. But a werewolf's power is obvious, inhuman, and transformative. <br /> <br /> Werewolf was translated into Lunars for the early Exalted setting. Solars and Terrestrials filled a niche sort of like Magi, in that they were the same sort of people they used to be, except incredibly good at what they did - including being good at being tough. Abyssals were sort of vampiric, but still basically people who are good at the gothy things they did. Lunars were semi-rescued from purely antagonist status, which was a disappointment.<br /> <br /> People have already mentioned the mechanical gaps between how cool Lunars coulda-shoulda-woulda been in 2E, so I'll leave that be.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I feel strongly about Lunars for 3E for several reasons.<br /> <br /> Solars and Terrestrials are still the characters who are the same sort of people they always were - just more competent and powerful. Lunars open up story space for characters who literally transform. There's quite a bit of fantasy transhumanism built into the idea here, that the Lunar changes themselves to adapt to the situation, and makes those changes a part of their continuing self. There's no reason why that transformation would be purely physical, either, or purely animal based. <br /> <br /> For example, a Lunar story could begin with a first transformation, showing the horror of having your body rip and stretch and rearrange itself into a new and awkward form. Then, with a little practice, the Lunar would get better at it, gain a few more forms, and start expanding her repertoire. She would live as other people in villages and towns, taking those forms with her when she leaves - here's a story about taking power at the cost to the innocent. <br /> <br /> She would live as the beasts when she hides away from civilization. She would learn what it means to be a bunny being stalked by a big cat, and also what it means to be the hungry big cat. Here's a story about perspective, for how scary could any number of humans be after that?<br /> <br /> She would experience the rage and Fury of the Fickle Lady, in a way that is poorly captured by Charm descriptions. Those would become part of her as well. She might craft a special shape engineered for war, or she might take the shapes and live the lives of gods, demons, or elementals. Here's a story about her battles, or her entry into strange worlds and planes of existence.<br /> <br /> She might eventually create the form of a giant kaiju. She would be so completely alien to anyone else, and equally alien to the young Lunar she once was, but by now this is as natural to her as changing clothes to anyone else. Here's a story where every old enemy seems so very small.<br /> <br /> The more of these things that incorporate into her nature, the smaller, more parochial, and more distant would seem the people of civilization. I think this is where the intent of Lunars as barbarians or as shapers of civilizations appears, though perhaps poorly captured in editions to date. <br /> <br /> Lunars would also be great candidates to join and adventure with any of the other splats. They could be the equal and complimentary mate to a Solar. They could walk incognito among the Dragon-Blooded. They could be the heavies to the lighter touch of the Sidereals. They could adventure with Abyssals in the Underworld or Infernals in Malfeas or Raksha in the Wyld. Each of these opens up as many story options for the Lunar as for the other, and a Lunar who returns from such an adventure is changed by it.<br /> <br /> Lunars aren't the only ones who change themselves, of course. Alchemicals and Liminals both do as well, and could partake in a different perspective on a lot of the same themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T07:01:27-08:00","id":1191909,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars#post1191798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why do people feel so strongly about them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Lunars are so popular because they are the Zero for the Solars' Megaman X. <br /> <br /> You know X is the central character, he is good and powerful... But who is this other guy with a different color pallete and... A plasma Sword!? <br /> <br /> This type of characters are always attractive. So Lunars are expected to be cool companions, and/or decent rivals. When their mechanics can't backup these themes, people usually demand changes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T09:02:40-08:00","id":1191954,"title":"","content":"Honestly, after recalling several of the talking points prompted by this thread and some of the extremes that some people have gone to, I've got to say that feeling <i>that</i> strongly about Lunars is not something that one should be sold on.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe developers have a solid vision of Lunars developed in the context of seeing several years of mistakes, and a good deal of mechanical and world-building acumen. I'd say they can be relied upon to deliver a solid, consistent product. Maybe it will be to your taste, maybe it won't, but I'd say that you should just leave it at that.<br /> <br /> \u200bDon't feel so strongly about Lunars. Don't identify with them so significantly that the question of any given mechanical or characterisation point can be a source of deep-seated personal outrage. Don't care about them enough to take commitments that both development teams have stuck to from the beginning as personal insults.<br /> <br /> It's really not worth it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T09:31:27-08:00","id":1191967,"title":"","content":"That is a really good post and I hope people take it to heart!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T10:36:30-08:00","id":1191989,"title":"","content":"Of course not. I'll gladly be enthusiastic to give them a good play, but it's not, nor should be, a sore point.<br /> <br /> Edit to add: I'm doing as much Lunar story space building as I can right now, because 3/5 of my players for our anticipated upcoming Ex3 chronicle want to play Lunars. We'll be starting with Solars for at least a short Story and to get everybody into the setting and rules, then decide if the homebrew is ready to play by then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":6192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","user":"Simon Darkstep","date":". 03-05-2018, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T13:56:55-08:00","id":1192052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1191816#post1191816\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bThat... is a complicated subject involving more than a decade of arguments and many positions that mix and match numerous points. It's difficult to elaborate on, or even summarise effectively.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe best that I can come up with is a list of some of the more noteworthy contentious points. (And by noteworthy, I mean things that I can manage to remember)<br /> <br /> There are:<br /> <br /> \u200b* people who dislike Heart's Blood shapeshifting, either wanting a more freeform kind ala characters such as Mystique, or just a method of acquiring forms besides hunting and killing (or for it to take front and centre).<br /> <b>* people who dislike the animal association.</b><br /> \u200b* people who dislike the Solar association.<br /> \u200b* people who think that a conflict with the Realm is nonsensical.<br /> \u200b* people who think that the setting should be filled with the results of Lunar nation building, crowding out the Realm.<br /> * people who think they should be reigning princes of the Wyld, drawn back to Creation solely by the return of the Solars.<br /> <b>\u200b* people who want the shapeshifting to lean more towards the fantastical or alien.</b><br /> * people who primarily want to focus on them as a kind of mirror Exalted.<br /> <b>\u200b* people who want them to have established princedoms throughout all of the realms of existence, and have a primary schtick about moving between them.</b><br /> \u200b* people who were really on board with the Thousand Streams River.<br /> <b>\u200b* people who wanted chimerism to be viable as a transhumanist path to ultimate power.</b><br /> <br /> And many more.<br /> <br /> I think you get the gist of it.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Excellent list.</i><br /> <br /> I just wanted to add that <b>many of these reasons are why the Infernal Exalted were beloved</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Pocket fiefdoms?</b> <br /> Rural tribes threatened by the Wyld? or custom-carved palace-kingdoms in Hell?<br /> <br /> <b>Armies? </b><br /> Half-naked Barbarians &amp; Beastmen? or endless, custom Demons races?<br /> <br /> <b>Warforms?</b><br /> Get ostracized for going Chimera? or custom-forms via BY RAGE RECAST?<br /> <br /> <b>Beastmen?</b><br /> Breed them and raise them for X-time? or use By Rage Recast to give loyal adult soldiers mutations?<br /> <br /> <b>Charms?</b><br /> Multiple &quot;like Solars - but weaker&quot; charms? or &quot;here's a completely sideways way to tackle an obstacle&quot;?<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd love to see Lunars revisited - but in many ways, Infernals slid into their role (the charm design alone was superb).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T15:12:56-08:00","id":1192075,"title":"","content":"My opinion? Lunars in 1e were a bit... lackluster. In 2e they were... generic feeling. This is both good and bad. As story elements they were adaptable! Flexible! Configurable! Able to be 50 different things to 50 different ST.<br /> <br /> As a result, we've now got completely different ideas about what the Lunars are about, what they SHOULD be about and how they should interact with the setting, and people being being, anything that is completely not compatible with that particular idea is clearly Wrong(tm).<br /> <br /> <br /> So from this, my prediction is that 3e Lunars is apt to be one of the most argued books in Exalted 3e. Because no matter which way the devs go, or even if they present options of going down Path A, but doing so reduces your ability to do path B and C, no matter how well they're written into the setting, it's going to get people upset because it doesn't match the vision THEY had for Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Odd_Canuck is not a topical medication or food product and is not to be taken internally or seriously.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/31-odd_canuck","name":"Odd_Canuck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar31_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1474"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T20:57:37-08:00","id":1192139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars#post1191798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't understand what about Lunars is such a point of contention for people. I've always seen them as... fine. They're OK. They're not my favorite Exalted. I don't hate them. They're just fine. I get the role they serve, I can come up with some character concepts for them, I think they have some neat aesthetics and themes.<br /> <br /> But why do people feel so strongly about them? What are they arguing about? How is &quot;Meerkat Steals The Spotlight Prana&quot; a thing?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I am sort of in the same boat as you. I have never really cared about Lunars all that much. Which honestly is a good thing. As you are seeing from the comments here people have very strong emotions on what Lunars should be. You have the chance that when they come out to approach it with a open mind without baggage. <br /> <br /> Sometimes indifference can be a blessing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-05T21:15:33-08:00","id":1192141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Snakesandsuns</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192139#post1192139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I am sort of in the same boat as you. I have never really cared about Lunars all that much. Which honestly is a good thing. As you are seeing from the comments here people have very strong emotions on what Lunars should be. You have the chance that when they come out to approach it with a open mind without baggage.<br /> <br /> Sometimes indifference can be a blessing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. At the same time, I possess an almost voyeuristic urge to observe flame wars and deranged, extreme opinions. This thread was my attempt to get a cliffnotes version of 15 years worth of rants and fanaticism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T00:29:07-08:00","id":1192166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192052#post1192052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Excellent list.</i><br /> <br /> I just wanted to add that <b>many of these reasons are why the Infernal Exalted were beloved</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah but the list for that would encompass most, if not all, of the traits of the other Exalted. They stole thunder from everyone - they had the villain cred of the Abyssals while also being shining protagonists of sorts, and the weirdness of the Sidereals' trees, along with living in a strange, alternate realm where they partied with everyone whenever they wanted, and they didn't have to worry about offenses against Celestial law getting them stuck under a mountain for a few centuries. They were like The Thing or The Blob of Exalted, which is probably why they seem to be getting trimmed back, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Pocket fiefdoms?</b><br /> Rural tribes threatened by the Wyld? or custom-carved palace-kingdoms in Hell?<br /> <br /> <b>Armies? </b><br /> Half-naked Barbarians &amp; Beastmen? or endless, custom Demons races?<br /> <br /> <b>Warforms?</b><br /> Get ostracized for going Chimera? or custom-forms via BY RAGE RECAST? </div> </div> </div>Taste and arbitrary numbers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Beastmen?</b><br /> Breed them and raise them for X-time? or use By Rage Recast to give loyal adult soldiers mutations? </div> </div> </div>This is pretty much the only break point. Breeding gets into weird FF7 Chocobo territory in a hurry, especially if you look at the multitude of bizarre schemes that people had for trying to make fast-reproducing populations in overwhelming numbers (none of which worked by the rules, but that stopped being the important part a long time ago).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Charms?</b><br /> Multiple &quot;like Solars - but weaker&quot; charms? or &quot;here's a completely sideways way to tackle an obstacle&quot;? </div> </div> </div>I voted for &quot;use the Alchemical Charms where possible&quot; toward the end, actually. It felt like it would work out pretty well at the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'd love to see Lunars revisited - but in many ways, Infernals slid into their role (the charm design alone was superb). </div> </div> </div>I can't agree with Infernals sliding into just their role, as, again, they were like a virulent infection trying to assimilate the setting with Yozi Charm bloat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-06-2018, 02:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T12:08:16-08:00","id":1192342,"title":"","content":"(Following may be tl:dr, but I'm trying to keep it fairly short and sweet)<br /> <br /> I might explain it like.... roughly, in 1e, of the original Exalted you had:<br /> <br /> a) Solars, who were the most powerful and got a lot of written adventures, hooks, fluff (some people would argue the setting and game was almost *purely* about playing Solars)<br /> b) Dragonblooded who were weak, but got a lot of written adventures, hooks, fluff (they got their own Aspect Books, Exalted: The Outcastes, and so on)<br /> c) Sidereals, who were in between Solars and Dragonblooded in power and had little setting material, but because they had a high concept, an imaginative sub setting and imaginative, tricksy Charms, were very popular online and had writers write memorable, cool things about them, and lots of cool fans saying awesome about them<br /> d) Abyssals, who were Solar tier, powerful and basically death-y Solars,<br /> e) Lunars.... who pretty much had none of these things, and wonky mechanics (and some political propositions about civilization and barbarism that some folks *really* hated).<br /> <br /> So, clamor for Lunars to be better mechanically, and have a high concept, and to be more written into the setting.<br /> <br /> This got stronger in 2e when the Infernals came out, and everyone got obsessed with both Infernals and pushing the envelope with complex Charm mechanics that were supposed to do weird yet high concept things that Said Things About Things in a grand way (whether or not Infernals actually did so wholly successfully being debatable). Charms that did classic, genre defining things were somewhat frowned upon, and 2e Lunar Charms were very much *not* high concept at all (many were scarcely even memorable)! And hence various homebrew reimaginings of the Lunars that sought to make them very high concept (and basically sort of like Infernals - Terrifying Argent Witches is one example of such homebrew).<br /> <br /> Things are probably more chilled out today, and it feels like people just want a Lunars that is generally true to their earliest inspirations, have a solid place in the setting and are well executed; rather than trying to make them a high concept thing that's away from their first origins in the setting and such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T12:47:43-08:00","id":1192352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192166#post1192166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Infernals) <b>stole thunder from everyone</b> - they had the villain cred of the Abyssals while also being shining protagonists of sorts, and the weirdness of the Sidereals' trees, along with <b>living in a strange, alternate realm </b>where they partied with everyone whenever they wanted, and they didn't have to worry about offenses against Celestial law getting them stuck under a mountain for a few centuries. They were like The Thing or he Blob of Exalted, which is probably why they seem to be getting trimmed back, too.</div> </div> </div> </div>My counter is they &quot;don't harm the coolness of other splats if they're inherently cool&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>My group loved Abyssals</b> - Infernals couldn't encapsulate &quot;ancestor-spirits, dead kingdoms, broken Neverborn tomb-bodies, love &amp; hatred beyond death&quot;, etc. Abyssals are tied to nostalgia, missed-opportunities, failure, etc - whereas Infernals are more a form of escapism, divorced from reality. Infernals don't face disappointed parent-ghosts, necromantically try to cleave to dead romance or get inspired by fallen heritage. Their <b>alternate realm</b> - the Underworld, Stygia and Neverborn tombs - was dope in a way Malfeas<i> could not emulate</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>The problem was other splats.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Sidereals?</b> There were no Infernals in 1st Edition - and yet, I still didn't want to play Sidereals - I didn't like their charms - and the only interest we ever had in Yu Shan was to maybe mass-murder the gods. Solars, Abyssals and Infernals all have a &quot;misfits that Creation spurns&quot; vibe that Sidereals <i>don't</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Infernals</b> didn't steal everyone's thunder - they <i>showed up with a complete package</i>. Your argument is akin to saying &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">that smart, attractive, successful person? damn them! if it wasn't for them, the &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">poor, ugly but smart</span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;, the &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">poor, dumb but sexy</span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot; and &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">dumb, ugly but rich&quot; </span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">groups would get laid more often!&quot; </span>Pre-Infernals, I'd stick with Abyssals and dodge the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192052#post1192052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Pocket fiefdoms?</b><br /> Rural tribes threatened by the Wyld? or custom-carved palace-kingdoms in Hell?<br /> <br /> <b>Armies? </b><br /> Half-naked Barbarians &amp; Beastmen? or endless, custom Demons races?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192166#post1192166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taste and arbitrary numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah.<br /> <br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Abyssals / Infernals / Sidereals / Terrestrials / Alchemicals</span>) can (command)<br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">ghosts / demons / gods / mortals / techno-mortals</span>) via their patrons<br /> (the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Deathlords / Yozis / Maidens / Houses / Cities</span>) and have &quot;home bases&quot; in the<br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Underworld / Malfeas / Yu Shan / Realm / Autochtonia</span>) - complete with the industrial support of<br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">undead craftsmen / craft-demons / craft-gods / Realm industry / <i>the-Craft-world</i></span>) to support their armies.<br /> <br /> See a pattern? <b>Lunars don't fit.</b><br /> <br /> They're the only Exalt-type whose <i>magical realm</i> is <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>trying to destroy them, both actively (the Fair Folk) and passively (the Wyld &amp; Bordermarches).</i></span><br /> <br /> They're the <i>most 2nd most <span style=\"color:#B22222\">inaccessible</span></i>. Too much Wyld wipes out your home - too little Wyld means that &quot;fast-travel-via-the-Wyld&quot; doesn't work - and if your &quot;territory&quot; is &quot;super stable&quot;, then enemy forces in Creation can meddle. Abyssals, Infernals, Sidereals all have parallel-worlds (with ways to cut through into them) and Terrestrials have an Empire that stretches across the map (so they can be located anywhere).<br /> <br /> They have the <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>most vulnerable followers</i></span>. Barbarians &amp; Beastmen do not have any special ability to withstand the Wyld - and they don't have the<i> infrastructure</i> with which to equip armies. They're raiders, scavengers and thieves at best.<br /> <br /> They have the <span style=\"color:#B22222\">most meddlesome</span> - and <span style=\"color:#B22222\">least influential</span> - &quot;patrons&quot;. Getting away from a Lunar Exalt is a <i>nightmare</i> compared to Abyssal &amp; Infernal patrons (who can't enter Creation), Sidereals (who are short-staffed and overworked - so you'll mostly deal with gods) or Dynastic Houses (who need their members &amp; lack Lunar mobility and stealth). <hr /><br /> I can have Wyld-flavored kingdoms near Oramus - or crazy-dream-environments via Hegra, the Typhoon of Nightmares - or hunt in the mirror-forests of Szoreny. Every Yozi is a potential surreal-landscape, many with the Wyld-themed beauty. And <b>thanks</b> to the Yozis themselves, I have potential patrons &amp; allies (demons) to prevent my HQ from being thoughtlessly destroyed.<br /> <br /> If Infernals didn't offer this, I <b>wouldn't</b> go back to playing Lunars - I'd ditch those landscapes altogether and go back to Abyssals.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192052#post1192052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Warforms?</b><br /> Get ostracized for going Chimera? or custom-forms via BY RAGE RECAST?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192166#post1192166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Taste and arbitrary numbers.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>Warforms:</b><br /> You are correct on &quot;taste&quot; here - although &quot;taste&quot; becomes the problem here.<br /> <br /> Abyssal groups were often open to diverse death-aesthetics; Infernal groups had 5-7 wildly different patrons to justify varying aesthetics; Lunars had this really weird tribalism (as Isator mentioned) where each group wants to convert the others to their interpretation of how Lunars should look (ironic for shapeshifters)!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Personal Anecdote:</b></span><br /> Years ago, I joined a large group online - focused around a city - where players could join different circles.<br /> <br /> I made a <i>Casteless Lunar</i> masquerading as an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Totem?</span> </b>Octopus - but instead of the <i>obviously animalistic</i> tentacle-cliche, I took camouflage &amp; poison mutations - so I can make my skin toxic and sickly looking.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Tell?</span> </b>Inspired by (2E Lunars, pg 130: the Tell &quot;of a Lunar may show up in his shadow&quot;) and (2E Abyssals, pg 155 - lvl 2 &quot;Branding&quot; Resonance: &quot;animating people's shadows as monstrous phantasms&quot;) - the ST approved &quot;ink-in-water style shadows, shifting like in water&quot;. It was <i>obviously magical</i> if noticed but not &quot;cat ears&quot;, etc.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Heartsblood?</b></span> My library was all deathly animals - the horse-sized corpse-skinned lamprey-mouthed maggots from Thorns; giant onyx-black centipedes; vultures; lizards that <i>shoot blood from their eyes</i>. I <i>never</i> shapeshifted into those forms - only using them for corpse-like mutations.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Anima? </b></span>Casteless anima banners are (silver, purple &amp; blue) &quot;hazy or distorted images of their spirit shape&quot; and Abyssal animas (in the Core) include (silver, purple, black, etc) &quot;horrible predatory, diseased or undead animals&quot;. I joined an Abyssal clique and blended it just fine with ink-blots &amp; tendrils alongside Daybreak &amp; Moonshadow animas. I even found a worthy &quot;Bond&quot;.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>...and then the Lunar players:</b></span><br /> <u><i>Not even a week</i>,</u> and <i>despite deliberately avoiding other Lunar players</i>, in come the PMs from people who <i>somehow</i> think I want to associate with them, they <i>think</i> I want the tattoos, they <i>think</i> it's <i>their duty to &quot;help&quot; me</i> (and all the while I wonder <i>how they even know my character is a Lunar when I don't interact with them</i>). By week 3, I couldn't go into the city without Lunar-players trying to identify me (wanting to RP is fine - giving me <i>special attention</i> you're not giving the Terrestrials, Solars, etc isn't).<br /> <br /> <b>I think Lunars are dope - </b>but if there was ever <i>anything</i> that discouraged me from playing them, it was the neo-tribalism of wolfboys and catgirls who think everyone wants to muck around in the jungle with a bunch of unwashed savages. Abyssal-bond, abyssal-circle, abyssal-attire and despite it all - <i>a couple of them</i> (the Lunars) became adamant that I had to join the Silver Pact (despite no in-character interactions to point them to me). If it's an online game, I rather play something else.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192166#post1192166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is pretty much the only break point. Breeding gets into weird FF7 Chocobo territory in a hurry, especially if you look at the multitude of bizarre schemes that people had for trying to make fast-reproducing populations in overwhelming numbers (none of which worked by the rules, but that stopped being the important part a long time ago).</div> </div> </div> </div>I had a separate thread on &quot;mortal games&quot; and it quickly spiraled into Half-Caste (which led to Beastmen and Breeding). I'm no stranger to bizarro land, lol.<br /> <br /> But yeah - flatly - By Rage Recast is much more effective than Beastmen Breeding (even though Lunars probably trump every other Exalt group in terms of designer-offspring).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192052#post1192052\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd love to see Lunars revisited - but in many ways, Infernals slid into their role (the charm design alone was superb).</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192166#post1192166\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't agree with Infernals sliding into just their role, as, again, they were like a virulent infection trying to assimilate the setting with Yozi Charm bloat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Different strokes is the best I can imagine here. Above I list an example where I think <i>the Silver Pact</i> was a virulent infection trying to assimilate all Lunars (no matter how much we don't want to join and have no interest in its aesthetics). Infernals let me play a shapeshifting demigod without the threat of being kidnapped and converted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 03-06-2018, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T13:19:51-08:00","id":1192365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192342#post1192342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">a) Solars, who were the most powerful and got a lot of written adventures, hooks, fluff (some people would argue the setting and game was almost *purely* about playing Solars)<br /> b) Dragonblooded who were weak, but got a lot of written adventures, hooks, fluff (they got their own Aspect Books, Exalted: The Outcastes, and so on)</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree the Caste/Aspect books really helped define an Exalt type in a spectrum from iconic through counter-to-type individual realities. Lunars, with such strong themes of identity to explore, were criminally underserved by having no Castebooks of their own. (Though I agree that books that don't make money are hard concepts to invest in - I think an omnibus would sell better, not the material itself to blame).<br /> <br /> So <a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/series/857280\" target=\"_blank\">I've attempted to correct that lack with fan-made Castebook</a>s using what writing and editing skill I could muster in my gaming group.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":1103,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","user":"Tikor","date":".  Spacing 03-06-2018, 04:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:02:33-08:00","id":1192384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192342#post1192342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Things are probably more chilled out today, and it feels like people just want a Lunars that is generally true to their earliest inspirations, have a solid place in the setting and are well executed; rather than trying to make them a high concept thing that's away from their first origins in the setting and such.</div> </div> </div> </div>That certainly seems to be what the devs are going for, from what they've said and the previews. They don't seem to be radically changing them; they're sticking with the animal-Lunars, not the protean mutants. <br /> <br /> Which is fine with me and my group; I always found all the arguments about how terrible Lunars were a bit odd, because everyone in my group liked Lunars and we always had a reasonable amount of Lunars in our game even though they were weaker than Solars. Not to say that there wasn't things we thought should be changed, but (sorry OP) no-one had giant flamewars about how terrible they were and why they should be changed radically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T14:20:55-08:00","id":1192392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192352#post1192352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My counter is they &quot;don't harm the coolness of other splats if they're inherently cool&quot;.<br /> <br /> <b>My group loved Abyssals</b> - Infernals couldn't encapsulate &quot;ancestor-spirits, dead kingdoms, broken Neverborn tomb-bodies, love &amp; hatred beyond death&quot;, etc. Abyssals are tied to nostalgia, missed-opportunities, failure, etc - whereas Infernals are more a form of escapism, divorced from reality. Infernals don't face disappointed parent-ghosts, necromantically try to cleave to dead romance or get inspired by fallen heritage. Their <b>alternate realm</b> - the Underworld, Stygia and Neverborn tombs - was dope in a way Malfeas<i> could not emulate</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Infernals had the Coolest Hell In Gaming as a backdrop. They fell into it, which gave them massive amounts of appeal right out of the gate. Even when the book got to treating interesting demons as merely potential ingredients, they still had their apartments and assemblages and all of the named demons.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>The problem was other splats.</b> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. It's like Autochthonians in 1e not giving Alchemicals terrible mechanics just because it was written in 2004, released in 2005, while Lunars was written in 2001, and released in 2002. And this was merely the first time it happened - 2e had to find its feet all over again rather than having them grounded at the beginning. A &quot;revised&quot; edition really shouldn't have to deal with nearly so much spitballing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Sidereals?</b> There were no Infernals in 1st Edition - and yet, I still didn't want to play Sidereals - I didn't like their charms - and the only interest we ever had in Yu Shan was to maybe mass-murder the gods. Solars, Abyssals and Infernals all have a &quot;misfits that Creation spurns&quot; vibe that Sidereals <i>don't</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>Infernals</b> didn't steal everyone's thunder - they <i>showed up with a complete package</i>. Your argument is akin to saying &quot;<span style=\"color:#0000CD\">that smart, attractive, successful person? damn them! if it wasn't for them, the &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">poor, ugly but smart</span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot;, the &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">poor, dumb but sexy</span><span style=\"color:#0000CD\">&quot; and &quot;</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">dumb, ugly but rich&quot; </span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">groups would get laid more often!&quot; </span>Pre-Infernals, I'd stick with Abyssals and dodge the rest. </div> </div> </div>No, my argument is that it threw a lot of bait everywhere. Often, they were in places that had mechanical shortcomings previous to that. Other material for 2e... was not usually so lucky to get an enthusiastic and well-written treatment such as this.. Even the Lunar Charms, which did at least sync up with the system, were split apart from lots of flavor that they should have had because of Eclipse Charm share fears. This came up later, when Holden noted that Lunar Charms being less than stellar didn't mean that Alchemical Charms had to be bad as well. And so, for the second edition, they became a kind of signpost for how Lunar Charms should have been.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, that got cut back big time for EX3. Eclipses no longer poach the powers of any other Exalted; just a few spirit Charms here and there. So we can have Lunar Charms that incorporate bestial shapeshifting again. Presumably, everyone is also on the same page about atmosphere and enthusiasm for writing the subject.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Abyssals / Infernals / Sidereals / Terrestrials / Alchemicals</span>) can (command)<br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">ghosts / demons / gods / mortals / techno-mortals</span>) via their patrons<br /> (the <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Deathlords / Yozis / Maidens / Houses / Cities</span>) and have &quot;home bases&quot; in the<br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Underworld / Malfeas / Yu Shan / Realm / Autochtonia</span>) - complete with the industrial support of<br /> (<span style=\"color:#0000FF\">undead craftsmen / craft-demons / craft-gods / Realm industry / <i>the-Craft-world</i></span>) to support their armies.<br /> <br /> See a pattern? <b>Lunars don't fit.</b><br /> <br /> They're the only Exalt-type whose <i>magical realm</i> is <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>trying to destroy them, both actively (the Fair Folk) and passively (the Wyld &amp; Bordermarches).</i></span> </div> </div> </div>As i've posted before on past threads, the cosmos does not hand out cool kids clubhouses as a matter of course. Lunars don't have one because they got ousted from the Realm but didn't roll over and die from it, instead starting a very long-view guerrilla war. Their purpose is to make Creation as uncomfortable and hazardous a place they can for Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals, and they've managed to destroy an awful lot of the cards that those two held prior to a millenium and a half of war. Once all the cards are gone, they have the advantage; their powers don't require much, if any, infrastructure to devastate the enemy, while on the other hand, the infrastructure of the Solars has been the only thing allowing the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals to survive and exercise control.<br /> <br /> But people really like cool kids clubhouses. So they fixate on that, and often insist that Lunars should have one, but that doesn't make sense given the setting. They're a rebellion hiding in the enemy's midst, not a fully organized hierarchy roughly symmetrical to the Realm or the Bureau of Destiny. Insisting that they be one is grand scale missing the point, which prior editions unfortunately ended up doing, with squatting out in the Wyld or trying to be Silver Sidereals with the TSR. Strike down another mistake gone for EX3; Lunars are in Creation, making Sidereals sweat and being what everyone thinks of when someone says &quot;Anathema&quot; with no qualifiers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They're the <i>most 2nd most <span style=\"color:#B22222\">inaccessible</span></i>. Too much Wyld wipes out your home - too little Wyld means that &quot;fast-travel-via-the-Wyld&quot; doesn't work - and if your &quot;territory&quot; is &quot;super stable&quot;, then enemy forces in Creation can meddle. Abyssals, Infernals, Sidereals all have parallel-worlds (with ways to cut through into them) and Terrestrials have an Empire that stretches across the map (so they can be located anywhere).<br /> <br /> They have the <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>most vulnerable followers</i></span>. Barbarians &amp; Beastmen do not have any special ability to withstand the Wyld - and they don't have the<i> infrastructure</i> with which to equip armies. They're raiders, scavengers and thieves at best. </div> </div> </div>Lunars engage in asymmetric warfare. Their forces aren't equipped traditionally because the enemy would just capture the base of infrastructure and use it for their own purposes. Which, again, is a point that comes up in EX3, and has been a part of conversations with various developers since 2012. So they sneak up on others instead. Though, beastmen in E3 actually get a one-point bump up on Might to help, too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They have the <span style=\"color:#B22222\">most meddlesome</span> - and <span style=\"color:#B22222\">least influential</span> - &quot;patrons&quot;. Getting away from a Lunar Exalt is a <i>nightmare</i> compared to Abyssal &amp; Infernal patrons (who can't enter Creation), Sidereals (who are short-staffed and overworked - so you'll mostly deal with gods) or Dynastic Houses (who need their members &amp; lack Lunar mobility and stealth). <hr /><br /> I can have Wyld-flavored kingdoms near Oramus - or crazy-dream-environments via Hegra, the Typhoon of Nightmares - or hunt in the mirror-forests of Szoreny. Every Yozi is a potential surreal-landscape, many with the Wyld-themed beauty. And <b>thanks</b> to the Yozis themselves, I have potential patrons &amp; allies (demons) to prevent my HQ from being thoughtlessly destroyed.<br /> <br /> If Infernals didn't offer this, I <b>wouldn't</b> go back to playing Lunars - I'd ditch those landscapes altogether and go back to Abyssals. </div> </div> </div>No, Lunar patrons have actually never been anything but hands-off. Even the most tightly-knit presentations of 2e didn't really make them very sticky or demanding. There were some factions that didn't really work or come into being how factions are supposed to work or come into being, and membership in them is strictly optional. In 1e, meanwhile, there was no stricture requiring a Mentor Background, either.<br /> <br /> [quote]<br /> <b>Warforms:</b><br /> You are correct on &quot;taste&quot; here - although &quot;taste&quot; becomes the problem here.<br /> <br /> Abyssal groups were often open to diverse death-aesthetics; Infernal groups had 5-7 wildly different patrons to justify varying aesthetics; Lunars had this really weird tribalism (as Isator mentioned) where each group wants to convert the others to their interpretation of how Lunars should look (ironic for shapeshifters)!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Personal Anecdote:</b></span><br /> Years ago, I joined a large group online - focused around a city - where players could join different circles.<br /> <br /> I made a <i>Casteless Lunar</i> masquerading as an Abyssal.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Totem?</span> </b>Octopus - but instead of the <i>obviously animalistic</i> tentacle-cliche, I took camouflage &amp; poison mutations - so I can make my skin toxic and sickly looking. </div> </div> </div>Those would probably be the ones most taken today, given how social media presents the cuttlefish's mimicry capabilities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Tell?</span> </b>Inspired by (2E Lunars, pg 130: the Tell &quot;of a Lunar may show up in his shadow&quot;) and (2E Abyssals, pg 155 - lvl 2 &quot;Branding&quot; Resonance: &quot;animating people's shadows as monstrous phantasms&quot;) - the ST approved &quot;ink-in-water style shadows, shifting like in water&quot;. It was <i>obviously magical</i> if noticed but not &quot;cat ears&quot;, etc. </div> </div> </div>2e Tells were terrible in proscription and mechanical execution. 1e Tells were actually better, in that they allowed oddities such as backwards bending hands or single eyes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Heartsblood?</b></span> My library was all deathly animals - the horse-sized corpse-skinned lamprey-mouthed maggots from Thorns; giant onyx-black centipedes; vultures; lizards that <i>shoot blood from their eyes</i>. I <i>never</i> shapeshifted into those forms - only using them for corpse-like mutations. </div> </div> </div>What corpse-like mutations? Those are scavengers. Corpses are food, not friends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Anima? </b></span>Casteless anima banners are (silver, purple &amp; blue) &quot;hazy or distorted images of their spirit shape&quot; and Abyssal animas (in the Core) include (silver, purple, black, etc) &quot;horrible predatory, diseased or undead animals&quot;. I joined an Abyssal clique and blended it just fine with ink-blots &amp; tendrils alongside Daybreak &amp; Moonshadow animas. I even found a worthy &quot;Bond&quot;.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>...and then the Lunar players:</b></span><br /> <u><i>Not even a week</i>,</u> and <i>despite deliberately avoiding other Lunar players</i>, in come the PMs from people who <i>somehow</i> think I want to associate with them, they <i>think</i> I want the tattoos, they <i>think</i> it's <i>their duty to &quot;help&quot; me</i> (and all the while I wonder <i>how they even know my character is a Lunar when I don't interact with them</i>). By week 3, I couldn't go into the city without Lunar-players trying to identify me (wanting to RP is fine - giving me <i>special attention</i> you're not giving the Terrestrials, Solars, etc isn't). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the writing left a lot to be desired in 2e. And people still stuck with it, because it was what was published. That's part of why we have a new edition.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>I think Lunars are dope - </b>but if there was ever <i>anything</i> that discouraged me from playing them, it was the neo-tribalism of wolfboys and catgirls who think everyone wants to <b>muck around in the jungle with a bunch of unwashed savages.</b> Abyssal-bond, abyssal-circle, abyssal-attire and despite it all - <i>a couple of them</i> (the Lunars) became adamant that I had to join the Silver Pact (despite no in-character interactions to point them to me). If it's an online game, I rather play something else. </div> </div> </div>Wow. Just... wow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Different strokes is the best I can imagine here. Above I list an example where I think <i>the Silver Pact</i> was a virulent infection trying to assimilate all Lunars (no matter how much we don't want to join and have no interest in its aesthetics). Infernals let me play a shapeshifting demigod without the threat of being kidnapped and converted. </div> </div> </div>Never has it been, even in 2e. Else, Vert wouldn't have been able to get away from the other Lunars to be the Casteless sig simply by, according to her writeup in SoE, basically yelling at them and telling them to fuck off. The present edition, though, doesn't mess around with presenting Dragon-Blooded organized together as serious threats, and there's no individual bond to anyone like in 2e (it's strictly opt-in like in 1e), so the dimensions of play might shape up a bit differently.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:05:18-08:00","id":1192411,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tikor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192365#post1192365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree the Caste/Aspect books really helped define an Exalt type in a spectrum from iconic through counter-to-type individual realities. Lunars, with such strong themes of identity to explore, were criminally underserved by having no Castebooks of their own. (Though I agree that books that don't make money are hard concepts to invest in - I think an omnibus would sell better, not the material itself to blame).<br /> <br /> So <a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/series/857280\" target=\"_blank\">I've attempted to correct that lack with fan-made Castebook</a>s using what writing and editing skill I could muster in my gaming group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like a nice little project and well worth it!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192384#post1192384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which is fine with me and my group; I always found all the arguments about how terrible Lunars were a bit odd, because everyone in my group liked Lunars and we always had a reasonable amount of Lunars in our game even though they were weaker than Solars. Not to say that there wasn't things we thought should be changed, but (sorry OP) no-one had giant flamewars about how terrible they were and why they should be changed radically.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe your group was pretty ahead of the curve (or behind it in the right way).<br /> <br /> ....<br /> <br /> Looking at some more posts on this page, every 2e related thread eventually turns into an Infernals thread.<br /> <br /> Just on Infernals and 2e, to comment on it, one of the weird things that strikes about Infernals in 2e, as characters is that the hell that sort of formed around them by implication, was kind of big and loud and gonzo and rockstars and pimp and indulgent and lurid and cocaine and hookers. But that seems kind of unapt, in hindsight, to how Jenna M wrote Malfeas in the first place. So I wonder if 3e can make Infernals who feel more like the Malfeas they live in and belong in is more like Games Of Divinity's.<br /> <br /> (Comment over, as this really ought to be talking about the Lunar Exalted if anything).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:29:59-08:00","id":1192429,"title":"","content":"I played a casteless Lunar for about 4 years of our game and wasn't worried about being kidnapped and forced to join the Silver Pact. Mostly my character's adopted daughter just whined &quot;dad, you'll turn into a Chimera unless you get tattoos!&quot; (which I did not, just got a few mutations).<br /> If other people had bad experiences with Lunar players though, fair enough.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But people really like cool kids clubhouses. So they fixate on that, and often insist that Lunars should have one, but that doesn't make sense given the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the key thing is Lunars kind of do have somewhere to live, but it's not the Wyld.<br /> It's the Threshold. You mentioned that they're trying to make it inhospitable to the Realm, but it's very hospitable to Lunars (where isn't?). <br /> <br /> It's not where Abyssals, Sidereals, Infernals or Dynastic Dragonblood generally live, they're coming to the Threshold from other places, but it's where Lunars live and thrive.<br /> <br /> I mean, if you look at the famous NPC Lunars:<br /> Raksi lives in a library;<br /> Magnificent Jaguar lives in a pyramid;<br /> Ma-Ha-Suchi lives in a nameless lair;<br /> Tamuz lives in a secret base somewhere in a large city;<br /> Leviathan lives around an ancient sunken city.<br /> <br /> None of them actually live in the Wyld, because that's not the Lunars' clubhouse, that's where Raksha live. The Lunars' homebase is the non-Realm-controlled parts of the Threshold (so, most of it).<br /> <br /> Some examples from the game I ran:<br /> The Changing Moon's base was a hidden village of beastmen and kids being trained as ninjas, in the jungle. She could see and sense everything in it and nearby, and it was surrounded by magic plants that would make interlopers go insane.<br /> The Full Moon lived in the same jungle, in a large tower where he trained martial artists.<br /> <br /> In the game I play, the Changing Moon and her father (my character) live(d) in a suite of palatial rooms in the Pharoah's palace (because she convinced the Pharoah to accept her husband as his long-lost son).<br /> <br /> None of them would ever live in the Wyld. My No Moon went there a couple of times to mutate himself, but otherwise we rarely went near it. Why bother? That's the Raksha PC's thing, not us.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think the key thing to note is that the Wyld was the Lunars' homebase during the Shogunate (assuming that bit of canon remains, it may not). It's not now. Occasionally my players have met Lunar elders who live in wyld zones, but most don't.<br /> <br /> <br /> The other thing to note is that Solars don't have a clubhouse, don't have active support from a patron, and don't have their own super-special place, and they seem to do fine.<br /> It's important to remember that Lunars are the easiest splat to play in a mixed game with Solars, and that's part of why. Their powers are very different from Solars (a lot more than Abyssals or Dragonblood), but their place in the setting is closer to Solars than other splats are, which means they can easily be slotted into the same kind of games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 03-06-2018, 06:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T15:40:55-08:00","id":1192432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>&quot;Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Multiple &quot;like Solars - but weaker&quot; charms? or &quot;here's a completely sideways way to tackle an obstacle&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, this is definitely true. The Lunar knacks were nice and different, but the charms were mostly just copies of Solar charms with a higher cost, more prereqs, or a reduced power (instead of inflicting any emotion, you can inflict fear, etc).<br /> <br /> As much as I enjoyed playing a Lunar, their charmset was the second worst in the game (and Sidereals, as much as their charmset was poorly written rules-wise, at least had interesting charms). My Lunar character had almost as many spells and knacks as actual Lunar charms (not counting excellencies, 11 spells, 19 knacks, and 32 charms), despite how weak a lot of the knacks were, just because the charms were kind of dull). And I'd have bought more knacks if the book had more (there weren't that many to choose from).<br /> <br /> (Though it depend on what attribute. Stamina was very unique, Dex very similar to Solar charms.)<br /> <br /> Even if their 3e charms aren't amazing, I'm sure they'll be more interesting than that.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T16:09:31-08:00","id":1192444,"title":"","content":"I think <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"929\" data-vbnamecard=\"929\">Ghosthead</a> nailed it in mentioning that 1E was all about playing a Solar. The Infernals and Abyssals were deliberately written as twisted Solars to justify them as peer antagonists. That left DB's as junior antagonists that might still be dangerous in groups. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T17:05:48-08:00","id":1192463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192429#post1192429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If other people had bad experiences with Lunar players though, fair enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI don't want to knock large group online play as a general thing, but between this and a few other accounts that I've heard, it does seem to be a medium that facilitates a certain attitude of... enforcing canon uniformity, and exploiting in-character groups as a method of bullying that into newcomers who enter with a novel idea.<br /> <br /> \u200bI can see how that might turn one off, but I would encourage a person to not conflate the in-character group with the players who represented themselves as it.<br /> <br /> \u200bCertainly, Third Edition's attitude towards the Silver Pact right out of the gate is that they're neither interested in forcing the involvement of uninterested parties, nor would they be capable of doing so.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-06T22:58:08-08:00","id":1192521,"title":"","content":"I hope you know how much I enjoy thought-out replies like this.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192392#post1192392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately, that got cut back big time for EX3. Eclipses no longer poach the powers of any other Exalted; just a few spirit Charms here and there. So we can have Lunar Charms that incorporate bestial shapeshifting again. Presumably, everyone is also on the same page about atmosphere and enthusiasm for writing the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ooooo.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192392#post1192392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As i've posted before on past threads, the cosmos does not hand out cool kids clubhouses as a matter of course. Lunars don't have one because they got ousted from the Realm but didn't roll over and die from it, instead starting a very long-view guerrilla war. Their purpose is to make Creation as uncomfortable and hazardous a place they can for Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals, and they've managed to destroy an awful lot of the cards that those two held prior to a millenium and a half of war. Once all the cards are gone, they have the advantage; their powers don't require much, if any, infrastructure to devastate the enemy, while on the other hand, the infrastructure of the Solars has been the only thing allowing the Dragon-Blooded and Sidereals to survive and exercise control.<br /> <br /> But people really like cool kids clubhouses. So they fixate on that, and often insist that Lunars should have one, but that doesn't make sense given the setting. They're a rebellion hiding in the enemy's midst, not a fully organized hierarchy roughly symmetrical to the Realm or the Bureau of Destiny. Insisting that they be one is grand scale missing the point, which prior editions unfortunately ended up doing, with squatting out in the Wyld or trying to be Silver Sidereals with the TSR. Strike down another mistake gone for EX3; Lunars are in Creation, making Sidereals sweat and being what everyone thinks of when someone says &quot;Anathema&quot; with no qualifiers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you a great deal - and I guess I'll have to wait to see their charms.<br /> <br /> The &quot;lesser Solar&quot; charms were problematic, because any threat that could kill a Solar would (by extension) seem capable of killing a Lunar. If <i>everyone on the map</i> has &quot;clubhouses&quot; (and armies and patrons and etc), it just seems like a gross disadvantage to have inferior charms AND the least resources.<br /> <br /> Maybe 3E charms. I never had a chance to play Alchemicals, so I only have vague familiarity with their mechanics - but Infernals were amazing at the &quot;disrupt areas&quot; schtick without needing heavy patronage. Beastmen are dope - but if Lunars had <b>By Rage Recast</b>, you could quickly twist an entire town into monsters. I always liked the idea of some Immaculates visiting a town - only to realize the &quot;noble families&quot; are all werewolves or something - but mechanically, this would involve Beastmen (with a mutation to hide other mutations; and then you have to <i>raise them</i>, educate them, build a town or steal one, etc). Infernals also had some She Who Lives In Her Name charms that were amazing for sweeping in and reorganizing human behavior.<br /> <br /> But without the mechanical &quot;umpf&quot;, yeah, cool kids clubhouses.<br /> <br /> Being the &quot;eternally on the run&quot; Exalts isn't bad, but has other issues (like how do you find peers - and why would you stick together). The &quot;cool kid clubhouses&quot; weren't just about power - they were ways to short-hand expectations. It wasn't &quot;<b>the Deathlords give us stuff!&quot;</b>, it was &quot;<b>the Deathlord we all serve kind of gives us a unifying theme for a circle&quot;</b> (whether it be the FaFL's conquest of the South; the Silver Prince's naval adventures &amp; politics; etc). Which Dynastic House, which Bureau you worked for, etc all helped orient games. <b>By not having this</b>, I feel like you end up with a generic Silver Pact - followed by &quot;every Lunar pulling in different directions because we all join with different expectations&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the Abyssal circle I played with, most of us served The Lover Clad. That - alone - was great &quot;short-hand&quot; for what kind of adventures we sought (which are wildly different from say, the Dowager's use for Exalts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192392#post1192392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunars engage in asymmetric warfare.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about <i>building things</i> tho?<br /> <br /> I'm not saying warfare isn't important - but most fight <i>to protect or build something</i>. That's another use for the &quot;cool kids clubs&quot;. I mean, I didn't see much of a resolution for Lunars until Glories of Luna gave us those pocket-dimensions (so Lunars can sort of hide their stuff). Or maybe if we used a Spirit (and hijacked a mobile sanctum somehow).<br /> <br /> Sure, the Elders might want to see the Realm wrecked - but I don't. Maybe I just want to live in luxury, masquerading among Patricians.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192392#post1192392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those would probably be the ones most taken today, given how social media presents the cuttlefish's mimicry capabilities.<br /> <br /> 2e Tells were terrible in proscription and mechanical execution. 1e Tells were actually better, in that they allowed oddities such as backwards bending hands or single eyes.<br /> <br /> What corpse-like mutations? Those are scavengers. Corpses are food, not friends.<br /> <br /> Yeah, the writing left a lot to be desired in 2e. And people still stuck with it, because it was what was published. That's part of why we have a new edition.<br /> <br /> Wow. Just... wow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Answering these altogether:<ul><li><b>Totem:</b><br /> Yes, these mutations may be common - but my point is, it's not the obvious &quot;I look like Ursula&quot; or &quot;I want to be a wolf-dude&quot;. A lot of Lunar players seem to love their werewolves, centaurs, harpies, etc - I specifically wanted to <i>not</i> be obviously half-animal.</li> <li><b>Tell: </b><br /> I agree with you on 1E &gt; 2E, although I'm not complaining - again, my example is simply &quot;I'm not obviously half-animal&quot;.</li> <li><b>Heartsblood &amp; Corpse-Like:</b><br /> You're correct that corpses are &quot;food, not friends&quot; - but I'd take anything that emulate Abyssal body-horror. I don't remember my old list, but off the top-of-my-head, here are some I recall and some I'd consider (I forget if they were on the old list).<ul><li><b>Fangs</b> - easy fit alongside Abyssals.</li> <li><b>Poison</b> - subtle, easy fit</li> <li><b>Corpse-like skin</b> - Camouflage (via octopus) or just a thick hide (with the appearance of the giant maggots who are described as being grotesquely pale, veiny, etc.</li> <li><b>Lamprey-hands</b> - If &quot;bird-Lunars&quot; don't automatically lose their arms in order to grow wings - and &quot;medusa&quot; Lunars can grow multiple snake-heads in their hair - then why should I suffer similar constraints? I forget if it was the giant-maggots, the lamprey or both - but at one point, I asked to turn my fists into maws full of teeth so I could bite targets via punching (mechanically, just claws). One ST was cool with Lunar body-horror (and I wooed a couple Abyssals who saw), another ST was less open to horrific-Lunars (so I avoided shapeshifting with them).</li> <li><b>Black Chitin-Armor</b> - Giant centipedes provide segmented armor - but then I photoshopped a mock-up, depicting my pre-existing clothing - to show how I covered the joints, etc. The goal was to make it look like &quot;polished black armor&quot; or even &quot;chitin armor from a dead giant-centipede&quot;, not something I grew.</li> <li><b>Bone Claws</b> - Central African Hairy Frogs break their own bones - to pierce their toes - to create claws.</li> <li><b>Ribcage Spikes</b> - Spanish ribbed newts push their ribs through their skin as defensive weapons</li> <li><b>Internal Organs</b> - Sea Cucumbers can vomit up their (stick &amp; toxic) organs and regenerate them. Maybe I take damage, but a few spare guts would be worth the stunt.</li> <li><b>Death scent</b> - I rad that opossum's (when afraid) emit corpse-like smells (to enhance their act).</li> <li><b>Blood</b> - Texas Horned Lizards emit blood from their eyes. Two snake species (Natrix Natrix &amp; Tropidophis) both secrete blood from their mouth, nose and eyes when disturbed (to play dead).</li> <li><b>Human Teeth</b> - The sheepshead fish has humanoid teeth.... but no lips. Grab this (instead of fangs) just for a smile to make the Joker cringe.</li> </ul></li> <li><b>2E Writing to be Desired:</b><br /> Agreed! But this wasn't about the writing. This was <i>player decisions</i> (even though they had no in-character knowledge of what my Exalt was). <b>Ergo</b>, this is <b>not </b>&quot;bad writing led characters to behave badly&quot;, it was &quot;bad players - <i>who like the writing</i> - using out-of-character knowledge to pursue a &quot;deviant&quot; they want to convert&quot;.</li> <li><b>Unwashed Savages:</b><br /> I'm being hyperbolic, but reminiscing on how <i>pushy</i> they were is just infuriating.</li> </ul><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <i>I think </i><i>the Silver Pact</i><i> was a virulent infection trying to assimilate all Lunars</i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192392#post1192392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never has it been, even in 2e. Else, Vert wouldn't have been able to get away from the other Lunars to be the Casteless sig simply by, according to her writeup in SoE, basically yelling at them and telling them to fuck off. The present edition, though, doesn't mess around with presenting Dragon-Blooded organized together as serious threats, and there's no individual bond to anyone like in 2e (it's strictly opt-in like in 1e), so the dimensions of play might shape up a bit differently.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fond of Vert, although I don't remember if Scroll of Exalts was out when this game ran. And the cover of the 2E Lunar book only has the 3 Castes. Here are some snippets from a quick search:<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#008000\">pg 35 warns &quot;Some Casteless may last longer than others, but <b>chimerism is the eventual doom of any Lunar </b>who lacks the protection of the tattoos.&quot; and describe a Casteless Lunar - Malik Fenn - by adding &quot;(Elders) <b>watch him closely for signs of chimerism</b>. They are coming to regret their decision...&quot;<br /> <br /> pg 112 on Castes, says &quot; In the Time of Tumult, only three castes remain, and <b>some unfortunate Moonchildren remain Casteless&quot;</b><br /> <br /> pg 120 on Associations &quot;<b>being Casteless is seen as a temporary state</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> pg 199 on Casteless admits &quot;The Silver Pact holds<b> no consensus</b> about such Casteless Lunars. A <b>narrow majority </b>says the Pact should leave Luna\u2019s Bastards to find their own way. Forcing a caste upon them would only mean resentful Lunars, which wouldn\u2019t help the Pact.&quot; and &quot;<b>Other Pact members say that all Unblooded should be tattooed whether they want it or not, </b>to save them from becoming chimerae.&quot; and then &quot;. <b>A very few Lunars, however, try to kill these \u201carrogant pups\u201d before the Wyld has a chance to taint them and hope the Pact can get them in their next incarnation.</b>&quot;<br /> <br /> pg 200 &quot;Unblooded Lunars do not yet know how to drink the heart\u2019s blood of animals or people and so are limited to their true forms. They might not have learned any Charms or Knacks. The Silver Pact <b>regularly sends retrieval packs to rescue Unblooded </b>when such missions seem likely to succeed. Virtually all Unblooded accept being marked with \u201cthe blood of Luna.\u201d Indeed, after listening to horror stories about chimerae from their rescuers, most Unblooded d<b>on\u2019t even consider the option of remaining Casteless</b>&quot; and &quot;Of course,<b> this assumes that tattooing is presented as an offer instead of a demand.</b> Some Silver Pact Lunars are so paranoid about chimerism that they try to <b>force tattoos on all Casteless, </b>regardless of the other Lunars\u2019 desires. This requires <b>browbeating, threats or use of Charms to force compliance</b>, and typically results in a very angry Lunar&quot; and &quot; Indeed, one disadvantage to Castelessness is the<b> lack of respect the Casteless receive</b> from Silver Pact Lunars&quot;<br /> <br /> pg 203 &quot; While individual members of the Silver Pact may<b> view a Casteless Lunar with excessive Wyld mutations as a chimera and try to kill her, a true chimera is a </b>Casteless Lunar who accumulated 10 points of permanent Limit and fell into a state of permanent Limit Break.&quot;</span><br /> <br /> <b>These are just a handful - but <i>as written</i> - it all adds up to Silver Pact Lunars:</b><ul><li>send retrieval pacts for the Casteless<ul><li>wont mention the possibility of staying Casteless<ul><li>may use charms to manipulate you into not being Casteless<ul><li>may use brute force to tattoo you anyways</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Remain casteless despite this? Silver Pact Lunars see you as...</b><ul><li>doomed eventually</li> <li>unfortunate</li> <li>weaker (mechanically enforced)</li> <li>temporary</li> <li>arrogant</li> <li>not respectable</li> </ul><b>And as a result, they will...</b><ul><li>spy on you<ul><li>regret respecting your decision<ul><li>kill you sooner (who cares about the &quot;narrow majority&quot; who spares you - you just need 1 motivated Lunar from the other side who disagrees and quietly kills you)</li> <li>kill you later (for looking too mutated, even though you're not Chimera)</li> </ul></li> </ul></li> </ul><b>Altogether, Castelessness is not a &quot;peer&quot; (like Vert) to be respected.</b> You're more an &quot;ignorant threat to yourself&quot;, and an opportunity for renown-seeking Lunars to &quot;recruit a novice&quot; (thereby establishing their steps to no longer being at the bottom of the social hierarchy).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192429#post1192429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I played a casteless Lunar for about 4 years of our game and wasn't worried about being kidnapped and forced to join the Silver Pact. Mostly my character's adopted daughter just whined &quot;dad, you'll turn into a Chimera unless you get tattoos!&quot; (which I did not, just got a few mutations). If other people had bad experiences with Lunar players though, fair enough.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was an online group - those are often dice-rolls in and of themselves. And like I said, I was lucky enough to have an Abyssal clique (so no need to kidnap).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192463#post1192463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI can see how that might turn one off, but I would encourage a person to not conflate the in-character group with the players who represented themselves as it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192429#post1192429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the key thing is Lunars kind of do have somewhere to live, but it's not the Wyld. It's the Threshold. You mentioned that they're trying to make it inhospitable to the Realm, but it's very hospitable to Lunars (where isn't?). It's not where Abyssals, Sidereals, Infernals or Dynastic Dragonblood generally live</div> </div> </div> </div>You make a good point, but the problem remains?<br /> <br /> <b>Vulnerability:</b><br /> Anywhere on the map, an Abyssal can engage in mass-murder to create a Shadowland (there's even one inside a cave on the Blessed Isle). And there is a Necromancy spell to cut into the Underworld. Infernals have similar methods via artifact keys and knives. Sidereals too. So it feels like <b>they</b> can all sort of &quot;teleport in and out&quot; from their pocket-dimensions - while Lunars feel exposed? Solars can try to raid these forgotten cities - but they generally can't just walk up to Malfeas and rob an Infernals' private stash.<br /> <br /> <b>Travel:</b><br /> Turning into a bird is useful? But Abyssals can cheat via the Labyritnhe; Sidereals via Yu Shan; Infernals via the strange travel time of Cecelyne's sands. We're talking about teleportation-gates and space-time-bending-Primordial-bodies.<br /> <br /> <b>Elders:</b><br /> Finally, as a <i>young Lunar</i>, the very same Elders you mention feel like they own all the cool stuff worth owning. They have <i>massive</i> territories. And Elders can go anywhere you can on the map if they disapprove of your behavior. It just feels like a better deal to go Abyssal or Infernal (patrons who can't follow you - so <i>they bribe you with cool stuff </i>to keep you coming back).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192432#post1192432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Lunar character had almost as many spells and knacks as actual Lunar charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Same, lol. My Lunars were collages of spells and mutations that used charms as little as possible (because if I wanted charms, I should play a Solar with some shapeshifting hearthstone for my face). Or I'd try to spend my motes by attuning to a ton of artifacts (in effect, serving as &quot;permanent charms&quot; for armor and the like).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 03-07-2018, 09:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T00:25:03-08:00","id":1192546,"title":"","content":"Just to note, Salagmisin: the incredibly elaborate manner in which you've been writing these last several posts makes them extremely difficult to quote.<br /> <br /> And also kind of bewildering to read...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192521#post1192521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What about <i>building things</i> tho?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bGiven the way that the developers have talked about Lunars, they're definitely going to have Charms to create things, and interact with societies in a positive manner.<br /> <br /> \u200bI won't speculate as to the form and limits those might take, as I carry my own biases to it, and know that I'm not exactly on the same page with the developers on all things Lunar (which I have absolutely no issue with).<br /> <br /> \u200bBut I'll note that the circumstances, if not the capacity, in which Lunars build things needs to at least make sense with where the setting is placing them. They ought to build things in a manner that takes advantage of why they need to engage in warfare against the Realm and Sidereals specifically, rather than render it irrelevant.<br /> <br /> \u200bSuddenly, I'm picturing an application of that idea the prior developers once presented, about building things that could be easily broken down afterwards; where the Lunars might face enemies such as the Fair Folk, in which overwhelming superior force actually is useful and preferable, but where it would be preferable to not leave these things intact for the Realm to come and take them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T00:44:42-08:00","id":1192548,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#ff0000\">Salagimsin, please refrain from using red text in your posts, it's forum etiquette that the mods use red text to convey statements made in their capacity as moderators. You should stick to simpler formatting on your posts, as stated above your current writing style is distracting rather than clarifying. Also, each post also doesn't need to take up half a forum page.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T06:10:17-08:00","id":1192587,"title":"","content":"Thankfully, hybrid forms now allow so much more variation in how a Lunar looks. It doesn\u2019t need to look vaguely animal-like, depending on which of the few Supernatural Merits you wish to express.<br /> <br /> Eska\u2019s hybrid form is more of a deva/asura appearance despite her totem being a Wolf Spider.<br /> <br /> I could make a Japanese oni by expressing only the horns of an ox and the fangs and claws of a tiger. I wouldn\u2019t even need to make those claws retractable, and I could choose for the skin to be red or blue, just as Eska\u2019s hybrid form is white.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s the basis of everything people loved about the Malfeas mutation Charms.<br /> <br /> Lunars will also have the power to turn adult human beings into beastmen and animals. Definitely through Celestial sorcery, and probably also Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T06:54:30-08:00","id":1192594,"title":"","content":"In the spirit of the OP, I have an ask about selling me also:<br /> <br /> Can someone sell me on the idea that non-lethal and permanent form acquisition doesn't undermine the Lunars being monsters/predators first and foremost? I'm very attached to the idea that no matter how much your concept strays from predator/monster that there are some things that a Lunar just *is*, and making it so Lunars can acquire forms non-lethally is a real buzzkill for me. I want to like Lunars but I don't like this. Can anyone maybe help me change my mind?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T07:13:49-08:00","id":1192600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192594#post1192594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the spirit of the OP, I have an ask about selling me also:<br /> <br /> Can someone sell me on the idea that non-lethal and permanent form acquisition doesn't undermine the Lunars being monsters/predators first and foremost? I'm very attached to the idea that no matter how much your concept strays from predator/monster that there are some things that a Lunar just *is*, and making it so Lunars can acquire forms non-lethally is a real buzzkill for me. I want to like Lunars but I don't like this. Can anyone maybe help me change my mind?</div> </div> </div> </div>Seduction as a hunt is a common metaphor, if one with some uncomfortable undertones at times.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T07:45:49-08:00","id":1192605,"title":"","content":"Killing someone is always going to be the temptingly quick and easy way to take someone else\u2019s face.<br /> <br /> Alternative methods make it possible to take someone\u2019s face when they\u2019re too strong or well-protected to quickly and easily kill...<br /> <br /> But for those who are weak and vulnerable, the Lunar has to want to go to the same amount of effort to avoid killing as she would need for someone too strong to kill.<br /> <br /> So, how much do you value the life of the little people you seek to move among?<br /> <br /> Beyond such issues, Heart\u2019s Blood has untapped applications in the realm of people willingly giving their faces away to you in return for something. Maybe a bargain where you agree to do something in return, or maybe they simply want to give you a mystical channel that makes it easier to heal their wounds or hear their cries for help.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T08:25:55-08:00","id":1192614,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192600#post1192600\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seduction as a hunt is a common metaphor, if one with some uncomfortable undertones at times.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192605#post1192605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Killing someone is always going to be the temptingly quick and easy way to take someone else\u2019s face.<br /> <br /> Alternative methods make it possible to take someone\u2019s face when they\u2019re too strong or well-protected to quickly and easily kill...<br /> <br /> But for those who are weak and vulnerable, the Lunar has to want to go to the same amount of effort to avoid killing as she would need for someone too strong to kill.<br /> <br /> So, how much do you value the life of the little people you seek to move among?<br /> <br /> Beyond such issues, Heart\u2019s Blood has untapped applications in the realm of people willingly giving their faces away to you in return for something. Maybe a bargain where you agree to do something in return, or maybe they simply want to give you a mystical channel that makes it easier to heal their wounds or hear their cries for help.</div> </div> </div> </div>The central question I would ask is: Why do these get to be equivalent to murder, a permanent removal of a person? Why do these form acquisitions get to be permanent? I would have no problem with temporary form acquisitions in the veins suggested above and for the reasons above. I just think killing someone is in a league of it's own and it makes a statement that is where the permanent power lies. That statement to me is important to put the stamp of &quot;Lunars are monsters/predators&quot; at the end of the day.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T09:00:30-08:00","id":1192625,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192614#post1192614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The central question I would ask is: Why do these get to be equivalent to murder, a permanent removal of a person? Why do these form acquisitions get to be permanent? I would have no problem with temporary form acquisitions in the veins suggested above and for the reasons above. I just think killing someone is in a league of it's own and it makes a statement that is where the permanent power lies. That statement to me is important to put the stamp of &quot;Lunars are monsters/predators&quot; at the end of the day.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Whether it fits their themes, essentially. Lunars are predators, but that's not their only theme - they are warriors, tricksters and shamen, existing in symbiosis with the societies they engage with.<br /> <br /> And being a predator isn't limited to violence and consumption alone.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T09:15:33-08:00","id":1192634,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar636_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"636\" data-vbnamecard=\"636\">Sunder the Gold</a> - Thanks for pointing Eska out! There's so much new content, I'm continually surprised. She looks <i>awesome</i>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> &amp; <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11\" data-vbnamecard=\"11\">Darksider</a> - Sorry! I've been <i>psyched </i>since I joined (I'm used to Reddit formatting). I had no clue about the red (I just changed it). And I <i>just learned </i>the @ symbols are a thing here. <i>This is amazing</i>.<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192546#post1192546\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bBut I'll note that the circumstances, if not the capacity, in which Lunars build things needs to at least make sense with where the setting is placing them. They ought to build things in a manner that takes advantage of why they need to engage in warfare against the Realm and Sidereals specifically, rather than render it irrelevant.<br /> <br /> \u200bSuddenly, I'm picturing an application of that idea the prior developers once presented, about building things that could be easily broken down afterwards; where the Lunars might face enemies such as the Fair Folk, in which overwhelming superior force actually is useful and preferable, but where it would be preferable to not leave these things intact for the Realm to come and take them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some 2E Infernal charms that always felt like &quot;a model&quot; for the playstyle include:<ul><li><b>By Rage Recast</b> (give others mutations from your custom set)</li> <li><b>Chirality Prohibition Index</b> (to reshape behavior &amp; geometry in an area)</li> <li><b>Transcendent Desert Creature</b> (hard to track; double speed via<b> Sand-Slip Trick; </b>spiritual via <b>Withered Soul Wastes</b>)</li> <li><b>Footprints Like Heralds Focus</b> (Demons count as AoE areas for TDC - 3rd Circle Demons count <i>for miles</i>)</li> <li><b>Scoured Perfection of Form</b> (gives mortals Transcendent Desert Creature as an Abomination)</li> <li><b>Dim Irrelevancies Unveiled </b>(detect local magic users)</li> </ul>So for example, an &quot;Infernal Batman&quot; in Gotham-Nexus would be <i>faster, hard-to-track</i>, <i>resists environmental hazards</i> <b>because</b> of the corruption he fights against. DIU makes him <i>amazing</i> at detecting supernatural threats and FLHF (cynically) explains why &quot;Infernal Batman&quot; never wants to kill &quot;Demons&quot; (ie, Joker, Clayface, Mr Freeze). So long as you permit the major villains to escape periodically, you get <i>all your powers</i> within X miles around them (or better yet, a Manse-prison Arkham dead-center, so even while imprisoned you still benefit (Essence) miles around. And if &quot;Infernal Batman&quot; wanted to recruit Robin &amp; co, BRR &amp; SPoF help share the powers!<br /> <br /> Obviously, Infernal charms have built-in side-effects - caveats that ensure Batman <b>won't</b> be successful (unless he's willing to eventually forego the source of his powers - by eradicating all forms of desolation). <b>Likewise</b>, Lunars would need an equivalent cost to explain why they don't spam these powers everywhere.<ul><li><b>Maybe</b> a Resonance-like building-up and bleeding-out of Wyld energy to fuel BRR and CPI. Imagine if Casteless could mitigate or purge mutations by periodically inflicting the taint on Realm populations.</li> <li><b>Or perhaps</b> - reflecting the &quot;need to engage in warfare&quot; - a less murderous version of <i>Murder is Meat</i> (so the more they lash out against the Realm, the more fuel for mutative-hijinks. If Lunars can rip faces and power from their prey - why not try cannibalizing some Terrestrials (even if the benefits are fleeting)?</li> <li><b>Or a combination of the above.</b> Imagine if &quot;Lunars can hold (Essence) victims at once - holding their (combined-essence-score) as &quot;X&quot;. So they prey on some Terrestrials - and then somehow spend X to bind a Fair Folk locally (as an origin for Wyld-flavored CPI, BRR, TDC, etc). So a week after culling a half-dozen Immaculates, a satrapy gets rumors of Fair Folk (or something worse) corrupting the mortals, some kind of Wyld-leak from a haunted manse or (gasp!) one of the Anathema cursing the city...</li> </ul>Infernals are 1/6th the Lunar host size - but some of their charms are just <i>amazing</i> for &quot;get in, destabilize, thrive, corrupt, escape&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T09:20:12-08:00","id":1192636,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192625#post1192625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Whether it fits their themes, essentially. Lunars are predators, but that's not their only theme - they are warriors, tricksters and shamen, existing in symbiosis with the societies they engage with.<br /> <br /> And being a predator isn't limited to violence and consumption alone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Where comes the gravitas of murder/killing if you simply don't have to most of the time? I'm not OK with equivalence in a world where there is no coming back from the dead. Killing should be the only permanent option simply because it comes with no-backsies and certainly more long term consequences. I have no interest in predation if we are using it entirely as a metaphor to dress up powers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T10:01:33-08:00","id":1192650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192634#post1192634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">some of their charms are just <i>amazing</i> for &quot;get in, destabilize, thrive, corrupt, escape&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI agree. Not necessarily in the precise details, but they certainly do provide a strong example of how Charms can be used to present that kind of playstyle, and make it engaging and flavourful.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf for nothing else, the Second Edition Infernals Charm set can be thanked for really expanding ideas of what Charms can be and how they can provide play style. I honestly think that without Infernal Charms, there would be no Evocations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Can someone sell me on the idea that non-lethal and permanent form acquisition doesn't undermine the Lunars being monsters/predators first and foremost? I'm very attached to the idea that no matter how much your concept strays from predator/monster that there are some things that a Lunar just *is*, and making it so Lunars can acquire forms non-lethally is a real buzzkill for me. I want to like Lunars but I don't like this. Can anyone maybe help me change my mind?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not sure that I can, because I'm more or less on the same page as you, but I'll make a game attempt at it.<br /> <br /> \u200bI suppose one way to look at it is that, while the other methods are still there, they might tend to demand a lot more time and effort and attention from the Lunar. Having those options means that you get to make a choice to not kill, but that choice can also represent an opportunity cost (one that might even be wasted, since the social system still affords methods and options for characters to not succumb to the Lunar's influence, unless they put <i>even more</i> effort in, so it has the added question of being dependent on another). They may not need to kill, but if it's the most expedient option, then I'd say there's always an underlying tension for a Lunar of just how much they're willing to put in for the sake of another's life, when the simpler and more permanent option is waiting in the wings.<br /> <br /> I'd say that it <i>is</i> something that can play into an element of a Lunar balancing humanity with monstrosity. Not a hard mechanical thing like the possibility of vampire Frenzy, just a range of differently balanced options for a player to handle. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T11:01:08-08:00","id":1192669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192636#post1192636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Where comes the gravitas of murder/killing if you simply don't have to most of the time? I'm not OK with qqequivalence in a world where there is no coming back from the dead. Killing should be the only permanent option simply because it comes with no-backsies and certainly more long term consequences. I have no interest in predation if we are using it entirely as a metaphor to dress up powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I suppose, ultimately, Lunars just aren't Abyssals or Raksha.<br /> <br /> For them, the hunt is more important than the kill and consumption, such that the hunt can take forms that don't determine success or failure by the literal death and consumption of the prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T11:26:19-08:00","id":1192677,"title":"","content":"<b>Re: Murder for Shapeshifting</b><br /> <br /> Keep in mind how quickly some shapes become <i>useless</i>. Unless you live locally, once someone is missing a few weeks (or days or even mere hours), it throws the identities into the trash. Even &quot;a guard missing a few hours&quot; can end up fired (and the disguise goes to shit)<br /> <br /> <b>And even if you live locally</b>, you have to invest time in <i>keeping those identities valid </i>(what good is shapeshifting into a local merchant-prince if 15 minutes into a conversation, it becomes obvious you don't know where your funds are located, don't know your trade partners, don't know local norms, etc.<br /> <br /> Besides which, <b>where is the gravitas in murder?</b> Abyssals might face the dead - and themselves came close to being sent to early graves - but why should a Lunar <i>care</i>? <br /> <hr /><br /> Yes, I like the cannibalism and horror of Lunar shapeshifting - but it's hardly a <i>moral issue</i>. That feels like a concern of contemporary society.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T11:37:52-08:00","id":1192686,"title":"","content":"Even if you get the form to be a specific disguise, the different shapes are still useful. It's always useful to be able to adopt various different human forms just for general disguise purposes.<br /> <br /> For example, my Lunar can take the form of an Emperor (because we murdered and ate him so we could take over the government). We now live far away, but it's still useful to be able to turn into an aging-but-still muscular man who just looks very different from the No Moon's natural shape.<br /> <br /> Actually, the majority of human shapes I've seen Lunars use are for generic disguises, not to be specific people. That Emperor is one of only two forms I can remember where anyone wanted to impersonate a specific person (the other being the party's Night Caste).<br /> (Though formerly Changing Moons could impersonate people with their Anima Banner, and would generally use that for specific people; it doesn't last long, but as you said, you sometimes can't impersonate someone easily for a long time anyway. But that may not be the case in 3rd ed.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T12:24:08-08:00","id":1192706,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192636#post1192636\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where comes the gravitas of murder/killing if you simply don't have to most of the time?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bTo summarise my points in relation to this question, I would propose that the gravitas can come from the statement that in this case, you viewed that person or animal's life as being worth less than the time and energy it would have taken to use another method.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf a Lunar should happen to have a large number of human shapes (particularly if they're maintaining the narrative in which sufficient familiarity with a Lunar makes it a lot easier to suss out their identity, creating an incentive to have such a library), it raises the question of if they bothered to put in that time for all of them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For them, the hunt is more important than the kill and consumption, such that the hunt can take forms that don't determine success or failure by the literal death and consumption of the prey.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bAre you saying that the existence of non-murder options for acquiring shapes means that murder actually should be treated as an inferior method for doing so, to be completely superceded the first time that you acquire an upgrade Charm? <br /> <br /> \u200b</span></span></span></div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b><span style=\"font-family:helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:10px\"><span style=\"color:#252c2f\">where is the gravitas in murder?</span></span></span></b><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> Abyssals might face the dead - and themselves came close to being sent to early graves - but why should a Lunar </span></span></span></div><i>care</i><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">?</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bI think that ParanoiaCombo's point might be about it being treated seriously by players and observers, rather than characters.<br /> <br /> \u200bOne can play a character that is indifferent to murder, but that itself can convey the gravitas of the act when it crosses with our cultural perception of people that are indifferent to murder. </span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T12:54:34-08:00","id":1192723,"title":"","content":"I agree with you that shapes are &quot;generally useful&quot;. <br /> <br /> But after a dozen or two dead humans, you don't really <i>need </i>more (all of this presuming you're even bothered by collecting such shapes). They could even be ex-cons, Guild slavers or failed Wyld-Hunt types who tried to kill you (to alleviate any sense of guilt). Ergo, murder isn't a &quot;moral problem&quot; tied to shapeshifting - you'll eventually have enough faces (and excuses to take them) - it's just inconvenient after a point, because you already have 20 viable faces to wear, so <i>why bother? </i>The answer to that would be &quot;to adopt their lives&quot; - but even <i>that</i> requires time investment. <br /> <br /> So when people are concerned about predation (which I favor) - my question is &quot;what are you looking to get out of it?&quot; I like the tactical-challenge of not having Mystique-style shapeshifting (but that's it). Likewise, the &quot;how do I keep this persona <i>useful</i> and &quot;alive&quot; is a <i>tactical-challenge</i>, not an ethical one. And by extension, non-murderous shape-taking can have their own tactical-challenges and complications. <br /> <br /> <b>Or</b> people specifically like murder because something makes murder unique. But what?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T13:34:02-08:00","id":1192741,"title":"","content":"This isn\u2019t even addressing the issue that Robert said Lunars would have disguise powers, and Shaping the Ideal Form.<br /> <br /> They don\u2019t need to eat people just to look different.<br /> <br /> I appreciate @Salagimsim\u2019s point about how killing someone for their face eventually invalidates the use of that identity as a cover. It\u2019s another thing that emphasizes how murdering people for their face is the quick and messy path to Heart\u2019s Blood, with consequences for the Lunar\u2019s disdain and impatience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:53:06-08:00","id":1192785,"title":"","content":"I've created a monster.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Never not tired","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12001-the-nilbog","name":"The Nilbog","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12001_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"207"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T14:55:26-08:00","id":1192786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192785#post1192785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've created a monster.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least it started out as a Lunar thread. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T15:40:24-08:00","id":1192817,"title":"","content":"On Lunars and Heart's Blood, to try and articulate my incoherent notions on this, generally I'm not so keen on what feel like &quot;sacrifice powers&quot; like this, just in general. And that goes for Riding The Dragon and other such powers, as well as Heart's Blood.<br /> <br /> I expect Exalted to often be violent - they are kung fu demigods and Princes of the Earth, and, unvarnished, that implies brutality. But the type of violence that interests me about them is the type that is driven by the same forces that cause people to use violence - to kill that enemy, to make that person afraid of you, to defeat the ruler crushing your land, to get rid of that girl pursuing a vendetta against you because you murdered her dad, just because you *can* and *want* to, etc.<br /> <br /> So I think I'm a lot less interested in the sort of &quot;You have to kill someone or something to gain access to this loosely related power&quot; sort of Charm / magic violence that's removed from these normal human considerations and cause and effect on the use of violence.<br /> <br /> Now that probably just means I will remain more interested in Solars and Dragonblooded and most of the Sidereals than types of characters (Lunars, Infernals?) where sacrifice and predation and violence either fuel or else are inescapable side effects of powers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-07T19:29:02-08:00","id":1192922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192521#post1192521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The &quot;lesser Solar&quot; charms were problematic, because any threat that could kill a Solar would (by extension) seem capable of killing a Lunar. If <i>everyone on the map</i> has &quot;clubhouses&quot; (and armies and patrons and etc), it just seems like a gross disadvantage to have inferior charms AND the least resources.<br /> <br /> Maybe 3E charms. I never had a chance to play Alchemicals, so I only have vague familiarity with their mechanics - but Infernals were amazing at the &quot;disrupt areas&quot; schtick without needing heavy patronage. Beastmen are dope - but if Lunars had <b>By Rage Recast</b>, you could quickly twist an entire town into monsters. I always liked the idea of some Immaculates visiting a town - only to realize the &quot;noble families&quot; are all werewolves or something - but mechanically, this would involve Beastmen (with a mutation to hide other mutations; and then you have to <i>raise them</i>, educate them, build a town or steal one, etc). Infernals also had some She Who Lives In Her Name charms that were amazing for sweeping in and reorganizing human behavior.</div> </div> </div> </div>2e had lots of Exalted doing things way, way too easily on a large scale by its end. I'm fairly certain that we won't be seeing anything that could just pop out what might normally take an elaborate sorcerous working in the space of a scene or less.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But without the mechanical &quot;umpf&quot;, yeah, cool kids clubhouses.<br /> <br /> Being the &quot;eternally on the run&quot; Exalts isn't bad, but has other issues (like how do you find peers - and why would you stick together). The &quot;cool kid clubhouses&quot; weren't just about power - they were ways to short-hand expectations. It wasn't &quot;<b>the Deathlords give us stuff!&quot;</b>, it was &quot;<b>the Deathlord we all serve kind of gives us a unifying theme for a circle&quot;</b> (whether it be the FaFL's conquest of the South; the Silver Prince's naval adventures &amp; politics; etc). Which Dynastic House, which Bureau you worked for, etc all helped orient games. <b>By not having this</b>, I feel like you end up with a generic Silver Pact - followed by &quot;every Lunar pulling in different directions because we all join with different expectations&quot;.<br /> <br /> In the Abyssal circle I played with, most of us served The Lover Clad. That - alone - was great &quot;short-hand&quot; for what kind of adventures we sought (which are wildly different from say, the Dowager's use for Exalts. </div> </div> </div>The assumption is presumably that you'll have a good reason to hate the Realm, and that your feelings will be magnified by a long history of acrimony with the Shogunate. Because they've been trying to kill you for 1500 years or so, and that kind of thing leaves lasting impressions, to say the least..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What about <i>building things</i> tho? </div> </div> </div>They'd have to be portable and/or easily taken apart and hidden. Failing that, you'd have to destroy them before your enemies use them against you. This is the world in which Lunars have had to live.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm not saying warfare isn't important - but most fight <i>to protect or build something</i>. That's another use for the &quot;cool kids clubs&quot;. I mean, I didn't see much of a resolution for Lunars until Glories of Luna gave us those pocket-dimensions (so Lunars can sort of hide their stuff). Or maybe if we used a Spirit (and hijacked a mobile sanctum somehow). </div> </div> </div>I'm not personally expecting pocket dimensions to return. I can't really speak to anything authoritative, but it seems to be another thing that undercuts the efforts of other mystical paths to get there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, the Elders might want to see the Realm wrecked - but I don't. Maybe I just want to live in luxury, masquerading among Patricians. </div> </div> </div>EX3 core mentioned something along those lines. They're still going to be hunting you and trying to imprison or kill you, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Answering these altogether:<ul><li><b>Totem:</b><br /> Yes, these mutations may be common - but my point is, it's not the obvious &quot;I look like Ursula&quot; or &quot;I want to be a wolf-dude&quot;. A lot of Lunar players seem to love their werewolves, centaurs, harpies, etc - I specifically wanted to <i>not</i> be obviously half-animal.</li> </ul> </div> </div> </div><ul><li>Don't complain when bestial shapeshifters are obviously bestial shapeshifters in their hulk-out forms. Just saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div></li> <li><b>Heartsblood &amp; Corpse-Like:</b><br /> You're correct that corpses are &quot;food, not friends&quot; - but I'd take anything that emulate Abyssal body-horror. I don't remember my old list, but off the top-of-my-head, here are some I recall and some I'd consider (I forget if they were on the old list).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T03:56:29-08:00","id":1193040,"title":"","content":"Dang, I can't edit my post. Just so you know, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I'm pretty sure this forum breakage occurs when you use bullet points and they get quoted, I've seen it happen before so if you avoid doing that in the future, it should help prevent this problem in other threads!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Violet Green, Freelancer</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer","name":"VioletDreamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23657_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:21:35-08:00","id":1193060,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, now I remember: I've said this before!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1090988-you-don-t-have-to-join-the-silver-pact\u2026?p=1090994#post1090994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Consider Zion, from the<i> Matrix</i> films. You might decide, &quot;Hey, fuck these guys and their weird dance orgies&quot; after they free you from your tube, but <b>regardless of whether you side with them or not, the Machines are coming for you,</b> and getting some support and training ain't too bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T05:37:53-08:00","id":1193065,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23657_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23657\" data-vbnamecard=\"23657\">VioletDreamer</a> Oh wow. Noted! Thank you for sharing the insight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T07:42:10-08:00","id":1193115,"title":"","content":"A couple thoughts and potentially clarifying points. 1) if we accept both infernales and abyssals as destroyers (debateable). It is not the Realm that is their target, but rather the whole of Creation. The Lunars by contrast are targeting the Realm specifically, though only as means to get to their true targets: sids and Dragonblooded. As to the idea that\u2019s an individual lunar may not share those goals, it is true in the short term, until the lunar stops and considers that the sidereals will not stop until they are dead. Why? Because the sids are trapped in a prisoners delima with regards to the lunar exalted and thus must always assume that any increase in power of an individual lunar has a probability of being turned in them.<br /> <br /> My problems for lunars as protagonists is they as a collective don\u2019t seem to have a positive aspiration (as was termed earlier a clubhouse). When you are solely focused on negative aspirations, it limits the stories one can tell. Hopefully lunars\u2019 book will give them positive aspirations to go along with their negative ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:21:28-08:00","id":1193137,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193115#post1193115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problems for lunars as protagonists is they as a collective don\u2019t seem to have a positive aspiration (as was termed earlier a clubhouse). When you are solely focused on negative aspirations, it limits the stories one can tell. Hopefully lunars\u2019 book will give them positive aspirations to go along with their negative ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lunars, with their fierce commitment to autonomy, will probably, as an entire group, only share aspirations that are thrust upon them externally, such as opposing the Realm, imposed by the policy of the Wyld Hunt. Those tend to be negative, like 'stop messing with me, or I'll rip your throat out'.<br /> <br /> However, sub-groups of consensual membership, as previously defined by the factions, but could easily be expanded, <b>do have positive aspirations</b> they rally around (misguided or not, based on personal preference):<br /> Swords of Luna: Protect Creation from threats crawling out of the Wyld.<br /> Wardens of Gaia: Craft perfect beings from controlled Wyld exposure or beastman breeding. (carving out space for these beings by tearing down civilization gets too much attention IMO)<br /> Sun King Seneschals: Restore the Solars to their rightful rule over Creation.<br /> Crossroads Society: Preserve sorcerous lore in Lunar society.<br /> Winding Path: Promote the Thousand Streams River project, to craft mortal societies that can thrive without Exalted rulership.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:31:08-08:00","id":1193138,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar177_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"177\" data-vbnamecard=\"177\">TheCountAlucard</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23657-violetdreamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23657_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23657\" data-vbnamecard=\"23657\">VioletDreamer</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> - <i>I agree with all of you</i>.<br /> <br /> My point is that <b>unless &quot;</b>I'm playing an 800-year-old Lunar&quot; <b>then </b>&quot;I don't have an 800-year-old grudge&quot;. <br /> Whatever has happened since the Shogunate is irrelevant if my Lunar was born &amp; Exalted in the last 5 years (or less).<br /> Lunar &amp; Solar Exaltations get <i>the same scrubbing</i> and Solars don't hate the Wyld Hunt any extra.<br /> And Lunars <i>have it easier than Solars</i> on running around undetected. <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Nilbog</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars#post1191798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But why do people feel so strongly about them? What are they arguing about?</div> </div> </div> </div>To define the Lunar Exalted is to limit them (and therefore fail to describe them).<br /> <br /> Front-line Heroics without the blunt power of Solars<br /> Stealth &amp; Guile without the divine privilege of Sidereals<br /> War &amp; Horror without the outright villainy of Abyssals<br /> Transhumanism without waiting for Edition's end for Infernals<br /> <br /> This comic combines dreams &amp; shapeshifting:<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/sLoVk\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/sLoVk\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/sLoVk\" target=\"_blank\"> https://imgur.com/gallery/sLoVk </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:40:16-08:00","id":1193144,"title":"","content":"Hmm, I was ready to suggest that two general purpose Lunar discussion threads going on at once was redundant, but then I thought... the other one actually has a decent basis of speculation on their future at the moment, and for some of the discussion going on here to end up there would drown it out.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it should be kept here.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T08:55:33-08:00","id":1193153,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I think you are undervaluing the aspect of lunar mentorship/teaching in inculcating the concepts of hatred to the Realm. Remember, most lunars are exalted both in luna\u2019s presence and/or find themselves called to lunar domains right after exaltation, when the new Exalted is most impressionable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:02:28-08:00","id":1193157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193138#post1193138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My point is that <b>unless &quot;</b>I'm playing an 800-year-old Lunar&quot; <b>then </b>&quot;I don't have an 800-year-old grudge&quot;.<br /> Whatever has happened since the Shogunate is irrelevant if my Lunar was born &amp; Exalted in the last 5 years (or less).</div> </div> </div> </div>What happened in the past creates the context of the present, even if you lack the continuity provided by social interaction with the previous generation.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'd be uncomfortable citing the experience of certain groups germane to the point that are not my own, so I'll instead say that your point is a lot like suggesting that an Irish person of the early 20th century would regard the English plantations of several centuries prior to be completely irrelevant to them, and they're not; an Irish person of that time is living, to their detriment, in the world that English conquest made.<br /> <br /> \u200bThat being said, my impression of the setup provided in the corebook is that the ratio of Lunars in the Silver Pact to Lunars who focus their rage and passion on things of their own, personal interest aligns fairly closely to Lunars that are fairly young and those who have been living in the Age of Sorrows for a few centuries. That the Silver Pact is willing to wait on newly tattooed Lunars because of the decent expectation that after living for a while in the world that is made subservient to the Realm and Sidereals (not least because those groups make the destruction of Lunar Exalted a point of basic ideology), they'll start to see the merit in the Pact's mission statement.<br /> <br /> \u200bThis does not need to be the case for every Lunar. It certainly does not need to be the case for the Lunar that you would play.<br /> <br /> But it's the basis for this element of the setting, and it has validity.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim<br /> Lunar &amp; Solar Exaltations get [I</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">the same scrubbing[/I] and Solars don't hate the Wyld Hunt any extra.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've never really considered it before, but in this Edition, they might just not. Whatever the basis of reincarnated Exalted having their past life memories curated, it might be that Lunars and Solars actually do get a very basic difference from it. There have been enough references to the idea of new Lunars having vivid recollections of the Old Realm and the Usurpation.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To define the Lunar Exalted is to limit them (and therefore fail to describe them).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's a fancy thing to say, but when they need to be playable, or even consistently written when it's necessary to bring on freelancers, then no; don't define Lunars in terms of &quot;you can't ever really describe them, maaaaaaaaaaaan&quot;.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Front-line Heroics without the blunt power of Solars<br /> Stealth &amp; Guile without the divine privilege of Sidereals<br /> War &amp; Horror without the outright villainy of Abyssals<br /> Transhumanism without waiting for Edition's end for Infernals</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThis actually points at another really big issue with the line trying to figure out Lunars, and especially with all of the competing viewpoints of them in the fanbase; the arbitrary need to make it a kind of competition with the other Exalted, and the need to figure out something for Lunars like an unencrochable niche, a unique role in the (irrelevant) Primordial War, or a form of power that nobody else can approximate. It has a number of issues, not least of which is inaccurately describing other Exalted, and often pushing ideas of the Lunars that fail to cover what they have been or many people would like them to be.<br /> <br /> \u200bTo whit: blunt power is an inaccurate way of describing the Solar Exalted, <i>lacking</i> blunt power is an inaccurate way to describe the Lunar Exalted, and the premise that leads to such a discussion is at fault in the first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This comic combines dreams &amp; shapeshifting:<br /> <a href=\"https://imgur.com/gallery/sLoVk\" target=\"_blank\">https://imgur.com/gallery/sLoVk</a></div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat actually gives me a thought on how to describe some of the basic problems in things that people have wanted from Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe story of a person who goes among shapeshifting demons or fairies or whatever else and engages in a literal or metaphorical contest of shapeshifting is a story you can tell with a Lunar.<br /> <br /> It is not a story that you can <i>only</i> tell with a Lunar, it is not an <i>essentially</i> Lunar story, and it is not a specific or primary purpose of Lunar shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> \u200bNone of that makes it invalid as a story that you could tell with a Lunar.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T09:14:45-08:00","id":1193162,"title":"","content":"I can't effectively quote Saur Ops Specialist, but I will say that I actually disagree with his points contesting a desire to associate a Lunar with Underworld iconography, and think that some of them are a bit pedantic. To my eyes, whether it's a Lunar who wants to harness certain animalistic mutations as a means of disguise and infiltration with the Underworld, or who identifies with the Underworld strongly enough that they go in heavily for animals associated with death or the incorporation of mutations that capture that image, it's perfectly valid as a thing for a specific Lunar character to want to do and be.<br /> <br /> \u200bI wouldn't see it as a &quot;Lunars as walkers of all the worlds, and partaking in all of their natures&quot; thing, but I would see it as a possible path for the Lunar desire for freedom and pursuit of self-expression and identity. That Lunar might not specifically be <b>of</b> the Underworld, but they can still go there and look the part, I think. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ghosthead</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1192817#post1192817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I expect Exalted to often be violent - they are kung fu demigods and Princes of the Earth, and, unvarnished, that implies brutality. But the type of violence that interests me about them is the type that is driven by the same forces that cause people to use violence - to kill that enemy, to make that person afraid of you, to defeat the ruler crushing your land, to get rid of that girl pursuing a vendetta against you because you murdered her dad, just because you *can* and *want* to, etc.<br /> <br /> So I think I'm a lot less interested in the sort of &quot;You have to kill someone or something to gain access to this loosely related power&quot; sort of Charm / magic violence that's removed from these normal human considerations and cause and effect on the use of violence.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bThat's an interesting point, and worth considering.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe only point I would have in addition to it is that I think certain aspects of the Lunar milieu draw on world views and mythologies that I think could be said to be ones that actually <i>do</i> ascribe a certain power to murder in its own right, rather then as a means to an end, and that Lunars can benefit from being distinguished by including that element.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:00:19-08:00","id":1193185,"title":"","content":"Isator Levi, we all have contradictions in our thinking, but most of us keep them to separate posts. I'd like you to reconsider your perceived irrelevance of the Primordial War, based on your own example.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193157#post1193157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...a unique role in the (irrelevant) Primordial War...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193157#post1193157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is a lot like suggesting that an Irish person of the early 20th century would regard the English plantations of several centuries prior to be completely irrelevant to them, and they're not; an Irish person of that time is living, to their detriment, in the world that English conquest made.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say that the Exalted person of the Second Age of Man is living, to their benefit, in a world the Primordial War liberated.<br /> <br /> I will agree with your other point, though, that describing things as unique, or special, or different is less powerful and evocative than describing things <i>as they are</i>, even if that happens to overlap with some other spirit, or Exalt, or stranger being.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/10wrFXvyXnNjaFJ0XrHdIwce6rnG__0k9/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Sidereal Jumpstart</a> (3e fanwork Charmset)<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1DQXwMXm8G1IEYLl-SmuFgKGugeZxQL63/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Cascades</a> (the above in flowchart form)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1103-tikor","name":"Tikor","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1103_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"826"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:17:40-08:00","id":1193189,"title":"","content":"grrruurrorrrrrr keepitsimplekeepitsimplekeepitsimple<br /> <br /> \u200bThere have been people who were extremely ardent that Lunars needed to be designed around answering the question of what role they fulfilled in the Primordial War (with a caveat that it couldn't have a crossover with Solar and Sidereal Exalted), and at the very least in <i>that</i> context the Primordial War is not relevant, even before developers had an idea that the adaptive nature of Lunars has made them different things in different eras.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:32:09-08:00","id":1193193,"title":"","content":"Having so little engagement with the Ghosts of Editions Past, I don't know if my own feelings on the Lunars carry much weight. But I'd like to submit for consideration that there's a distinction between an archetype of killing or <b>murder</b>, and an archetype of <b>predation</b>. Murder is a net-loss for the universe: A victim is slain, and they will never be or do anything ever again. Predation is not necessarily a net loss: The blood of the stag becomes the strength of the pack. Sure, predation destroys something, perhaps as permanently as cold-blooded murder woiuld. But in a story about predation, something about the prey is preserved or passed on. Depending on one's perspective, you can talk about the stag becoming the wolf, or the wolf becoming the stag. You are what you eat, and so on.<br /> <br /> Predation being a process, and a transformative process, is what appeals to me about the theme or predation and its relation to Lunars. So, non-lethal methods of taking Heart's Blood don't necessarily seem problematic to me, so long as they live up to those themes: destruction, consumption, transformation. If you can take Heart's Blood by, say, taking all of a target's memories away. It seems fair to say that the prey has been forever removed from the world, and that what has been taken from them is now the predator's to possess. That which has been taken now empowers the predator. Or if you can manipulate a fanatic into abandoning their faith entirely, or seduce somebody away from the love of their lives, steal a singer's voice, or any number of other things, really.<br /> <br /> The mechanics of this edition seem to lend reasonable short-hands for establishing what you need to do to accomplish this kind of thing. What you do to them has to be dramatic enough to completely remove or replace one of their Defining Intimacies.<br /> <br /> What tack is taken with non-lethal forms of mystical predation in Lunars in this edition remains to be seen. But I don't think the presence of non-lethal options <b>has</b> to weaken the Lunar identity as ultimate predators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23633,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","user":"Catastronaut","date":". 03-08-2018, 01:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","name":"Catastronaut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:41:44-08:00","id":1193198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193189#post1193189\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">grrruurrorrrrrr keepitsimplekeepitsimplekeepitsimple<br /> <br /> \u200bThere have been people who were extremely ardent that Lunars needed to be designed around answering the question of what role they fulfilled in the Primordial War (with a caveat that it couldn't have a crossover with Solar and Sidereal Exalted), and at the very least in <i>that</i> context the Primordial War is not relevant, even before developers had an idea that the adaptive nature of Lunars has made them different things in different eras.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn\u2019t the role they play in the primordial war be that they were the champions of Luna? Isn\u2019t that all the Lunars have to be? That and it wouldn\u2019t matter what their role was in the primordial war was because the Lunar\u2019s themselves broke and remade themselves.<br /> <br /> One of the reasons I have never really cared for Lunars personally is because I am not particularly interested in shape shifters (although now that I could possibly play a horrible abomination kaiju that might change). However isn\u2019t that enough? Isn\u2019t that enough of a cool thing, the ability to turn into various animals, to warrant their inclusion. Why do Lunars need to be more than that? Not every exalt is for the same sort of story and as such does not need the same resources. If you aren\u2019t interested in that type of story you could just not play a lunar or have your lunar do their own unique stuff. Creation is vast and I am sure many areas have never heard of the realm or only think of the realm as a distant mythical land. I am sure those areas are unique play grounds for Lunars as well.<br /> <br /> (please note I am not necessarily commenting on your opinions Isator, just your comment got me to thinking).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2302-snakesandsuns","name":"Snakesandsuns","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2302_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"224"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T10:52:46-08:00","id":1193203,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't necessarily say that the need to kill people to get their faces means that Lunars have a <i>theme</i> of murder, but murder is definitely what they're doing when that happens.<br /> <br /> \u200bEven by the more poetic definitions you've given there: Eska of the Seven Blades doesn't strike me as the type to acquire shapes through trickery or seduction or bargaining, and she can assume the shapes of children. She has definitely murdered children, and they will never grow up, never experience a more full life, never contribute anything to their society. All that she got out of that was their faces, so that she could sneak up on people that she wants to fight.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:00:31-08:00","id":1193207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193144#post1193144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, I was ready to suggest that two general purpose Lunar discussion threads going on at once was redundant, but then I thought... the other one actually has a decent basis of speculation on their future at the moment, and for some of the discussion going on here to end up there would drown it out.<br /> <br /> So yeah, it should be kept here.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree. I'm still catching up to 3E, so it's safer to answer &quot;why do people feel strongly&quot; but not &quot;how do we move forward&quot;.<br /> <br /> And by the way - you post a lot - but man, you keep it interesting. I hope to be as brief-yet-effective as you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Irish person of that time is living, to their detriment, in the world that English conquest made </div> </div> </div>You are shrewd to wield history against me - my heart! I love these comparisons.<br /> <br /> But my quibble is <i>that Irish-Americans eventually assimilated into the majority</i>. Irish-Americans don't usually speak Irish anymore. Many aren't Catholic. Few (especially in the US) recall how Anglo-Americans considered them a &quot;sub-race&quot; and &quot;non-white&quot;. <b>Despite being raised from birthas &quot;Irish&quot;</b>, they have slowly seen that identity erode with each generation until now in the US they are merely &quot;white&quot;. This is actually something I see come up a lot in recent Jewish-American plays - preserving one's racial identity against assimilation into other foreign categories.<br /> <br /> <b>Am I suggesting Lunars will see themselves as Terrestrial Exalts? No. </b><br /> <br /> <b>But Lunars aren't raised from birth within &quot;the Silver Pact&quot;</b> - which is why I scream &quot;artificiality!&quot; A Solar &amp; Lunar duo from Sijan will <i>both be equally Sijanese</i> - another duo from Lookshy will <i>both be equally Lookshyan; </i>a duo from Nexus will have<i> Nexus-derived-values</i>. The &quot;Silver Way&quot; reeks of artificiality. You don't spend 20-30 years of life in a city - and then shed your identity after 3 months of a prolonged camping trip.<br /> <br /> <b>And linguistically, </b>Clawspeak just <i>sounds like an insult</i> to one's intelligence. Plus it's rarely spoken to outsiders - so what good is a cypher or psuedo-tongue that only 299 other souls <i>in all of Creation </i>can understand, if <i>statistically</i> there's little chance of meeting them <i>especially</i> if we live in a city. <b>Claw marks</b> in Chiaroscuro's architecture are more likely to attract the Wyld Hunt than to inform the 1-3 Lunars who <i>might</i> never walk those streets (I go back to my praise of <i>Dim Irrelevancies Unveiled &amp; co</i> - Infernals can find each other better). <br /> <br /> <b>I mean,</b> there are roughly 2,200 Billionaires according to Forbes - that's x7 as numerous as the Lunar Exalted - but would <b>anyone</b> pretend to Bill Gates, Xiang Wang, Daniela Sirtori-Cortina and Muhammad Cohen would sit together to learn &quot;Richspeak&quot; for the express purposes of only talking to each other? Are they going to claw-up the streets of New York, Dubai, Hong Kong and Madrid <i>for the off-chance</i> that one of the other 2,199 billionaires will <i>walk that specific street</i> and notice <i>that specific marking</i> and see <i>a <b>non-time-sensitive </b>message</i>? <br /> <br /> Imagine a claw up &quot;Danger&quot; on a certain neighborhood - but within a decade, that neighborhood's population and demographics changed (war, new migrants, better policing, name it). Do urban Lunars then apply spackling paste to fix the walls they disfigured?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> but in this Edition, they might just not. Whatever the basis of reincarnated Exalted having their past life memories curated, </div> </div> </div>This and everything else you wrote make me see how much more I need to read on 3E. They can't print fast enough!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saipjas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193153#post1193153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I think you are undervaluing the aspect of lunar mentorship/teaching in inculcating the concepts of hatred to the Realm. Remember, most lunars are exalted both in luna\u2019s presence and/or find themselves called to lunar domains right after exaltation, when the new Exalted is most impressionable.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not undervaluing &quot;lunar mentorship in inculcating hatred to the Realm&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm saying &quot;I don't need Silver Pact help to fight 800-year old grudges&quot;<br /> if I &quot;am not an 800-year-old Lunar who wants Silver Pact membership &amp; grudges&quot;<br /> <br /> <i>Casteless</i> Lunars <i>are the coolest</i> for me. As is.<br /> <br /> But they're the only splat to simultaneously combine:<br /> - &quot;you're mechanically inferior - <i>unless you join us</i>&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, our bosses give us rewards if we <i>rescue</i> you&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, stay rogue too long and you threaten yourself - we want to <i>save</i> you&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, stay rogue too long, you turn Chimera - we want to <i>save those around you</i>&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, we're just here to remind you the Realm <i>really hates you&quot;<br /> - &quot;okay, fine</i> - they got 300 Solar Essences to hunt - <i>but somehow they give you special attention&quot;</i><br /> - &quot;<i>okay, fine - </i><u>you're a shapeshifting demigod</u> - but they'll find you - somehow! <i>just join us, please</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> If Ma-Ha-Suchi &amp; Raksi needs lackeys in 50 years, they can retry me then! <br /> I don't play shapeshifters to have <i>less freedom</i> than a nascent Solar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:10:40-08:00","id":1193210,"title":"","content":"I certainly don't mean to say that Lunars should be regarded as anything other than horrifying murder-beasts in the eyes of most of Creation. Certainly many (most?) Lunars will have murdered to further their own goals, or even just to acquire a few more guises.<br /> <br /> I mostly meant to argue against the position that the mere existence of any other alternatives to murder necessarily undermines the archetype of the Lunar predator.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","name":"Catastronaut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:18:44-08:00","id":1193213,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> I understand where you are coming from. I\u2019m talking lunars as a collective not individual edge cases (which is where you seem to be coming from). I am mostly working from an in universe setting level not an individual narrative perspective. As an aside I would argue that sids would see lunars (generally) as a greater threat due to their unity. Even if an individual may have no care about it, as an antagonist group the sids would see a lone isolated lunar (especially a low essence lunar) as a juicy target. I think however this does not have to apply to your edge case IF the ST doesn\u2019t want it. But that is one of my issues overall which is all of this is ST dependent:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:18:54-08:00","id":1193214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Catastronaut</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193210#post1193210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I certainly don't mean to say that Lunars should be regarded as anything other than horrifying murder-beasts in the eyes of most of Creation. Certainly many (most?) Lunars will have murdered to further their own goals, or even just to acquire a few more guises.<br /> <br /> I mostly meant to argue against the position that the mere existence of any other alternatives to murder necessarily undermines the archetype of the Lunar predator.</div> </div> </div> </div>With this thought firmly in mind, I imagine writing Scenes in which the Lunar &quot;hunts&quot; her prey and takes a shape in a broader sense.<br /> <br /> Maybe she could hunt a courtesan by outdoing her popularity at court, or by sabotaging her age-staving cordial to render her ugly. Thus assuming her status and position rather than literally face and appearance.<br /> <br /> Maybe she could hunt a magistrate by exposing his corruption or letting a bunch of his past-convicts out of the gaol. Thus taking on his reputation and authority in the form of robes and seal. <br /> <br /> Just thinking out loud (out type?) while enjoying the thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:28:21-08:00","id":1193220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193214#post1193214\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[...]rather than literally face and appearance.<br /> <br /> [...]taking on his reputation and authority in the form of robes and seal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd replace &quot;rather than&quot; and &quot;in the form of&quot; with &quot;in addition to&quot;. Taking Heart's Blood, (at least as I understand it) allows the Lunar to take the form of their prey, before all else.<br /> <br /> My take on it is that by taking possession of these things, which are as crucial to the respective prey-humans as their own heart's blood, the Lunar takes, consumes, and transforms something of what would have otherwise been merely destroyed by the Lunar's machinations. This definitely allows the Lunar to take on their faces and forms, in addition to whatever else happens in the narrative.<br /> <br /> The analogy here would be that taking a mighty cave bear's Heart's Blood should give the Lunar an awesome bear-form, in addition to a big pile of bear meat. My conception of Lunars is that their magic makes the metaphorical/mystical very literal and visceral, so both things should happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","name":"Catastronaut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:30:02-08:00","id":1193221,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193207#post1193207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I hope to be as brief-yet-effective as you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Phhhahahahahahahhahahaha<br /> <br /> \u200bAh yes, I am infamously brief and to the point in my posts. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, for the other stuff, I'll say that of course history is big enough to contain counterexamples to any given thing in it. I'm not saying that the scenario presented in the books is the only possible one that they could go with.<br /> <br /> \u200bBut it's credible and creates compelling drama and hooks the Lunars directly into the setting (the lack of which has always been a major issue that the fans have had with them), and that makes it valid as an approach.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe cultural thing has a few aspects. When it comes to conflict in the Realm, those would include how whatever culture they belonged to before has probably also been detrimentally affected by the dominance of the Realm, and that there can be something to the methods employed by Lunars to those newly inducted into the Silver Pact to see merits in their agenda, especially when that's packaged in empowering and seductive narratives.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs a few writers have said, it's not necessarily a hard pitch to make when you're telling people that they're entitled to rule the world.<br /> <br /> \u200bAnother aspect to that is the question of just how much a given Lunar is attached to their native culture, when part of the criteria is being somebody who is a bit of an outsider or iconoclast, who struggles against constraints put on them socially. Not every Lunar will have the same answer to that, but it's a premise in which some, maybe a lot, will readily distance themselves from that old life.<br /> <br /> \u200bAs for Clawspeak, I have no idea if that will even still be a thing. I have some doubts, but there are a few arguments in its favour. It's still mostly a fringe element of Lunars.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Silver Way&quot; reeks of artificiality. You don't spend 20-30 years of life in a city - and then shed your identity after 3 months of a prolonged camping trip.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bHyperbole (and possible assumption that Lunars are still going to by ideological primitivists) aside, some people do. People join cults. Hell, there are Americans who have left everything they ever knew and lived with to go join ISIS.<br /> <br /> \u200bQuestion is, is there a selection bias in the people who are Exalted as Lunars that would make whatever attitude more apparent among them?<br /> <br /> And last, to break a few things down:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But they're the only splat to simultaneously combine:<br /> - &quot;you're mechanically inferior - <i>unless you join us</i>&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, our bosses give us rewards if we <i>rescue</i> you&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, stay rogue too long and you threaten yourself - we want to <i>save</i> you&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, stay rogue too long, you turn Chimera - we want to <i>save those around you</i>&quot;<br /> - &quot;actually, we're just here to remind you the Realm <i>really hates you&quot;<br /> - &quot;okay, fine</i> - they got 300 Solar Essences to hunt - <i>but somehow they give you special attention&quot;</i><br /> - &quot;<i>okay, fine - </i><u>you're a shapeshifting demigod</u> - but they'll find you - somehow! <i>just join us, please</i>&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bBeing given a Caste is not dependent on membership in the Silver Pact.<br /> <br /> \u200bThere is no longer a detriment beyond lacking Anima powers and Caste Attributes to being Casteless; degenerative chimerism is no longer a thing.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe background of the Silver Pact is based on a world in which Solars were mostly gone with no expectation of returning. I presume one can play a Lunar at character creation who has been active for a fair few years longer than their return, and that the Lunars book will address the subject of how the return of Solars changes expectations for the future of Lunars in the long term.<br /> <br /> \u200bLunars can shapeshift, but there's a question of what else they do. If you're never using your powers in a manner that has a possibility of getting the attention of the Realm and Sidereals, there's a question of how fulfilled that character is, and if they <i>are</i> doing so, there's a question of how far disguise will get you, especially when the opposition has powers of their own.<br /> <br /> Also, the Silver Pact really isn't going to be approached like an organisation now; more of a collective goal, and a network of favour trading.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:49:47-08:00","id":1193234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193221#post1193221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>I've gone from being angry at 2E to clamoring to buy 3E Lunars.<br /> Ugh. I need sleep. And a weekend of reading. Thanks for <b>all</b> the info. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:00:36-08:00","id":1193240,"title":"","content":"I bid 4 Solar XP for anybody mapping this thread as an Ex2 social combat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:11:33-08:00","id":1193245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193240#post1193240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I bid 4 Solar XP for anybody mapping this thread as an Ex2 social combat.</div> </div> </div> </div>I tried but at some point I drew my Daiklaive and accidentally my namesake<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> While having Lunars have the ability to acquire forms non-lethally doesn't undermine their themes of predation (thanks for pointing that out Catastronaut) , I think the line in what gives forms <b>permanently</b> is certainly a valid hill to die on when defending those themes. I'm perfectly fine with form acquisition from non-lethal sources existing as long as it's not permanent. I just draw the line at &quot;If you want this forever, someone has to die&quot;<br /> <br /> That at least maintains the drama of &quot;do I quick murder or go through a lot of work not to kill this person to get their form temporarily&quot;. It just seems to me like the presupposed &quot;easy/bad&quot; way to acquire forms should simply be more attractive because that's how you create internal conflict and drama. Killing being just &quot;easier&quot; isn't enough for me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":255,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","user":"ParanoiaCombo","date":". 03-08-2018, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:24:43-08:00","id":1193251,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193245#post1193245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the line in what gives forms <b>permanently</b> is certainly a valid hill to die on when defending those themes. I'm perfectly fine with form acquisition from non-lethal sources existing as long as it's not permanent. I just draw the line at &quot;If you want this forever, someone has to die&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>This seems reasonable, but is probably where we diverge. (De gustibus non disputandum est, and all that.) I think non-lethal sources are fine, even for permanent acquisition, so long as the action required constitutes, in some sense, a destruction of the person in question.<br /> <br /> Stealing the voice of a random peasant or bureaucrat: insufficient. Stealing the voice of a singer, renowned throughout three kingdoms for their golden voice: sufficient.<br /> Seducing a soldier in a tavern: insufficient. Seducing the scion of a noble family, literally born and raised to seal by marriage an alliance decades in the making, the night before the wedding: sufficient.<br /> <br /> And I don't think that all of these alternate modes of predation should be available to all Lunars by default. I think it only fitting though, that some such paths should be available to certain Lunars who express their predatory nature in different ways.<br /> <br /> I think it is fine for the path to Heart's Blood through killing to be the only path available to all Lunars, and for it to be a path that is always open to each and every Lunar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23633,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","user":"Catastronaut","date":". 03-08-2018, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23633-catastronaut","name":"Catastronaut","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23633_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T15:23:06-08:00","id":1193328,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193162#post1193162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can't effectively quote Saur Ops Specialist, but I will say that I actually disagree with his points contesting a desire to associate a Lunar with Underworld iconography, and think that some of them are a bit pedantic. To my eyes, whether it's a Lunar who wants to harness certain animalistic mutations as a means of disguise and infiltration with the Underworld, or who identifies with the Underworld strongly enough that they go in heavily for animals associated with death or the incorporation of mutations that capture that image, it's perfectly valid as a thing for a specific Lunar character to want to do and be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, if I could edit the point by point out now, I would. I was caught on whether or not I should have one instead of just mass-snipping and cutting to the point of Lunars being more mythic in EX3, but though that I could follow it up later. At least, follow it up easily and without much fuss.<br /> <br /> I still don't think that mutation effects are likely to look like worn armor rather than thick hide, exoskeletons and what have you, though, or yield corpse-like appearances. The former seems like it's some other Exalt's territory, and the latter seems to specifically be Liminal territory. If you have an association with the Underworld and you've gone whole-hog in diving into necromancy (now in the Onyx Circle!), I'm guessing that you just look like a foreboding example of your totem beast(s).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bI wouldn't see it as a &quot;Lunars as walkers of all the worlds, and partaking in all of their natures&quot; thing, but I would see it as a possible path for the Lunar desire for freedom and pursuit of self-expression and identity. That Lunar might not specifically be <b>of</b> the Underworld, but they can still go there and look the part, I think. </div> </div> </div>I'm suggesting that they look like something aside from ghosts, revenants, or Abyssals. Something that may look like it's at home there, but isn't any of the above, or actually dead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T17:05:59-08:00","id":1193362,"title":"","content":"Wait, before I get into anything else:<br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Don't complain when bestial shapeshifters are obviously bestial shapeshifters in their hulk-out forms. Just saying.</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> \u200bWell, there's no need to complain, because this is simply incorrect now. Eska of the Seven Blades' hybrid form barely looks bestial, and can easily be mistaken for something else. When she first showed up in the comic, people were uncertain if she even <i>was</i> a Lunar; I know I wouldn't have thought she was if she didn't turn into a bird at the end. That precedent is established, and it is perfectly valid for any future Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, give Eska's mutations to something other than Extra Arms and keep the skin tone, and she'd look damn corpse-like herself.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T17:16:48-08:00","id":1193364,"title":"","content":"Actually, Salagimsim, while I do agree myself that hybrid body mutations taking the form of something that resembles clothing or external armour is taking things a step too far, a Lunar could just wear soulsteel armour. They wouldn't be able to use it to its fullest power (unless it happened to have an additional basis for Resonance that the character fulfils), but they wouldn't be any weaker with it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T18:23:57-08:00","id":1193383,"title":"","content":"\u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193328#post1193328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm suggesting that they look like something aside from ghosts, revenants, or Abyssals. Something that may look like it's at home there, but isn't any of the above, or actually dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sidereals don't get Abyssal charms.<br /> <br /> But Black Ice Shadow - a Chosen of Endings - was marked for incarnation as <i>a Ghost-Blooded</i>, grew up in an Abyssal manse within a Shadowland and he <i>self-initiated into necromancy</i>. He wields <i>soulsteel short daiklaves</i>.<br /> <br /> Solars don't get Terrestrial charms.<br /> <br /> But Jencir of Chanos - a Night Caste in 1st Edition - was &quot;a loyal child of the Realm, member of the All-Seeing Eye&quot; before he Exalted. Are Solars prohibited from using the &quot;Gem of White Heat&quot; (Oadenol's, pg 94) that &quot;perfectly emulates a Fire-aspected Terrestrial animal power&quot;? Are Solars prohibited from wielding red jade or learning elemental-themed MA?<br /> <br /> I understand that &quot;superficial, broad, splat-specific aesthetics&quot; - <b>but in practice</b>, the edges exist to accommodate spy games. Why should Lunars be less-competent than Solars at stealth? <hr /><br /> <b>This is all about mimicry and emulation, not &quot;necrotic taint&quot;.</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>Pretend to be Abyssal?</b></span><br /> <b>Beast-Power Concentration</b> - let me use DBT powers while remaining human.<br /> <b>Subtle Chameleon Practice</b> - is a Permanent charm to prevent Peripheral essence.<br /> <b>Outland Navigating Guile -</b> lets me apply &quot;Wyld Sensing Instincts&quot; to the Underworld.<br /> ...and my &quot;<b>ink-blot shadow Tell</b>&quot; is magnified by BPC and emulates Resonance<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><b>Add more psuedo-Necromancy?</b></span><br /> <b>Wasp in the Labyrinthe Trick</b> - that lets me <i>animate corpses</i> via parasitic drones<br /> <b>Thousand Wasp Dance</b> - to vomit up insect swarms that bite people<br /> <b>Ash and Tears Banquet</b> - <i>lets ghosts become valid targets of the sacred hunt</i>.<br /> <b>Limb Shielding Growth </b>- grow forearm bone-carapace shields<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><b>DBT as Deathly Ubermensch?</b></span><br /> <b>Perfected Hybrid Interaction! </b>DBT requires &quot;animalistic features&quot; that &quot;represent the admixture of spirit shapes&quot; - but PHI only exists to &quot;<b>ignore DBT's guidelines</b>&quot; when picking mutations, with the psuedo-social-penalty that &quot;many Lunars consider this Knack a step along the road to chimerism and view its possessors with deep suspicion&quot; <b>Terrifying Beastman Alteration </b>then adds even more mutations.<br /> <br /> I can pick <b>subtle mutations</b> like &quot;Inexhaustible&quot; (Wyld, 146), &quot;Air Adaptation&quot; (Wyld, 145), Chameleon &amp; Toxin (Core, 289), &quot;Disgusting Scent - rotted meat&quot; (Lunars 207), . Altogether, a psuedo-zombie form that is <i>ice-cold, never tires, no sleeps, discolored skin, toxic bite, etc.</i><br /> <br /> I can pick <b>super crazy mutations</b> like the &quot;Stone Body&quot; (Abomination, Wyld, pg 148) - but instead of &quot;cooled lava rock, never melting ice&quot; etc - I manifest my armor as &quot;blood that drips from my pours and solidifies into sanguine-armor&quot; or &quot;eruptions of bone-plate&quot;. Add in fangs, broken-bones-as-claws, bone-carapace shields. <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">I don't have Abyssal Resistance charms </span>but I can do a hell-of-a-job emulating them!<br /> <br /> <b>Are these not all Lunar powers?</b><br /> <br /> At no point do I have the mechanics that Abyssals, Liminals, Chosen of Endings and similar splats have for their themes. <b>I'm just emulating them</b>. <b>Like my totem</b>. Because &quot;camo&quot; isn't just about blending in with the scene, <i>lots of animals</i> use camo to emulate more dangerous species.<br /> <br /> <b>And then</b> <b>I haven't even touched </b>death-flavored Martial Arts, Necromancy, Abyssal Hearthstonesm etc,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193328#post1193328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> though, or yield corpse-like appearances.</div> </div> </div> </div>As above, I'm not &quot;eating a zombie, looking like a zombie&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'm using a dozen death-emulating Lunar-powers and animal-mutations to <i>seem corpse-like</i>. There's an entire Wikipedia page dedicated to <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apparent_death\" target=\"_blank\">animals pretending to be dead</a> </b>as a survival mechanism. There's even a fish <b><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nimbochromis\" target=\"_blank\">look dead</a> </b>so it can then eat scavengers (and is &quot;evolving&quot; to favor more death-like colorations)..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193328#post1193328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing that you just look like a foreboding example of your totem beast(s).</div> </div> </div> </div>Except Perfected Hybrid Interaction lets me completely and forever ignore my &quot;spirit shapes&quot;. The octopus-as-spirit-shape can forever be a <i>spiritual</i> symbol (as my Lunar camos to hide amongst Abyssals) without <b>ever</b> needing to turn into <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gi58pN8W3hY\" target=\"_blank\">Ursula</a>.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193364#post1193364\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Salagimsim, while I do agree myself that hybrid body mutations taking the form of something that resembles clothing or external armour is taking things a step too far, a Lunar could just wear soulsteel armour. They wouldn't be able to use it to its fullest power (unless it happened to have an additional basis for Resonance that the character fulfils), but they wouldn't be any weaker with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193328#post1193328\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't think that mutation effects are likely to look like worn armor rather than thick hide, exoskeletons and what have you,</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you both &quot;in so far that&quot; I knew I should check with the ST first - to see how far we agree on the mutation.<br /> <br /> But &quot;chitin armor&quot; doesn't mutate my limbs either. I'm still human.<br /> <br /> And PHI specifically &quot;ignores DBT's guideliness&quot; - which includes &quot;animalistic features&quot; - so <b>with that</b>, I imagine the Stone Body Abominatoin (that is clearly non-animal) works. But instead of asking for &quot;hardened lava-plate or unmelting-ice hide&quot;, I'm still <b><i>going biological</i> </b>with blood or bone (like other Lunar bone charms) - or even <b>keeping</b> the black-chitin armor, but asking for PHI to &quot;bend and curve it&quot; to less literal interpretations.<br /> <br /> Check out this <a href=\"https://78.media.tumblr.com/d63e5693a8e6fc509ba7e984da41902e/tumblr_oaayzte9331tipvuzo3_1280.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Chitin Armor Cosplay </a>(from Morrowind). They used giant insects as pack-animals - and their hides as armor-plates. It's not quite what I went for but it conveys the idea of &quot;oh yeah, large bug-plate-armor.... but if I disguise the joints, they won't realize it's literally grown from my flesh&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or better yet, this <a href=\"https://farm5.static.flickr.com/4079/4893381874_700eb88c16_b.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">black centipede</a> and then <a href=\"https://gamer-mods.ru/_ld/37/90361915.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, <a href=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/0287/th/pre/i/2017/250/5/a/assassin_by_alexruizart-d7r0mc7.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>, <a href=\"https://pre00.deviantart.net/2c9e/th/pre/i/2014/168/a/7/dual_by_digitalsashimi-d7mulmw.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> and <a href=\"https://i.pinimg.com/originals/35/35/f6/3535f6457e63021f18bc5edb9a8c5a77.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. Full-body black-chitin as psuedo-plate. <b>Nothing</b> demands I need extra limbs or elongated bodies. <b>Or maybe</b> I build a warform of obsidian armor via &quot;pathwork&quot; of mutations. <b>I wish</b> I knew if/where I saved my character art. <br /> <br /> But TLDR - I don't expect to shapeshift full plate on. I'm totally down with biological themes like blood, bone or black chitin. I'm just <i>really big</i> on the idea of collaging mutations until no one can claim I'm &quot;a bug person&quot; (or if my human-bits will have side-effect mutations, I hide my face within a chitinous psuedo-helm altogether).<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Lesson Learned - don't google &quot;human centipede&quot; when seeking centipede armor ideas.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":". 03-08-2018, 09:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T19:58:39-08:00","id":1193400,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah. With the new Hybrid Body Transformation, I could choose a bug totem and have a <i>Guyver </i>or <i>Kamen Rider</i>-like battle form. Neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T00:48:46-08:00","id":1193463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Salagimsim</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Sidereals don't get Abyssal charms.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But Black Ice Shadow - a Chosen of Endings - was marked for incarnation as </span></span></span><i>a Ghost-Blooded</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, grew up in an Abyssal manse within a Shadowland and he </span></span></span><i>self-initiated into necromancy</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">. He wields </span></span></span><i>soulsteel short daiklaves</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">Solars don't get Terrestrial charms.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">But Jencir of Chanos - a Night Caste in 1st Edition - was &quot;a loyal child of the Realm, member of the All-Seeing Eye&quot; before he Exalted. Are Solars prohibited from using the &quot;Gem of White Heat&quot; (Oadenol's, pg 94) that &quot;perfectly emulates a Fire-aspected Terrestrial animal power&quot;? Are Solars prohibited from wielding red jade or learning elemental-themed MA?</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I understand that &quot;superficial, broad, splat-specific aesthetics&quot; - </span></span></span><b>but in practice</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">, the edges exist to accommodate spy games. Why should Lunars be less-competent than Solars at stealth?</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>Non-native powers using hearthstones, artifacts, and sorcery/necromancy are just that - not effects that derive from the Charm set of a character type. I've seen the same arguments involving general-use powers made to try and crowbar an astounding amount of material into being &quot;viable Solar Charms&quot;. Also, do we need to get into another discussion of Solars being the ne plus ultra at stealth because Stealth exists as an ability? Because that's been an established thing for a while. Don't try to slam your head into the wall like most of the 2e Lunars did, because it is not worth the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Pretend to be Abyssal?</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Beast-Power Concentration</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - let me use DBT powers while remaining human.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Subtle Chameleon Practice</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - is a Permanent charm to prevent Peripheral essence.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Outland Navigating Guile -</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> lets me apply &quot;Wyld Sensing Instincts&quot; to the Underworld.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">...and my &quot;</span></span></span><b>ink-blot shadow Tell</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot; is magnified by BPC and emulates Resonance</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000CD\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Add more psuedo-Necromancy?</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Wasp in the Labyrinthe Trick</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - that lets me </span></span></span><i>animate corpses</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> via parasitic drones</span></span></span><br /> <b>Thousand Wasp Dance</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - to vomit up insect swarms that bite people</span></span></span><br /> <b>Ash and Tears Banquet</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> - </span></span></span><i>lets ghosts become valid targets of the sacred hunt</i><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">.</span></span></span><br /> <b>Limb Shielding Growth </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">- grow forearm bone-carapace shields</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>DBT as Deathly Ubermensch?</b></span></span></span><br /> <b>Perfected Hybrid Interaction! </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">DBT requires &quot;animalistic features&quot; that &quot;represent the admixture of spirit shapes&quot; - but PHI only exists to &quot;</span></span></span><b>ignore DBT's guidelines</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">&quot; when picking mutations, with the psuedo-social-penalty that &quot;many Lunars consider this Knack a step along the road to chimerism and view its possessors with deep suspicion&quot; </span></span></span><b>Terrifying Beastman Alteration </b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">then adds even more mutations.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can pick </span></span></span><b>subtle mutations</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> like &quot;Inexhaustible&quot; (Wyld, 146), &quot;Air Adaptation&quot; (Wyld, 145), Chameleon &amp; Toxin (Core, 289), &quot;Disgusting Scent - rotted meat&quot; (Lunars 207), . Altogether, a psuedo-zombie form that is </span></span></span><i>ice-cold, never tires, no sleeps, discolored skin, toxic bite, etc.</i><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I can pick </span></span></span><b>super crazy mutations</b><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"> like the &quot;Stone Body&quot; (Abomination, Wyld, pg 148) - but instead of &quot;cooled lava rock, never melting ice&quot; etc - I manifest my armor as &quot;blood that drips from my pours and solidifies into sanguine-armor&quot; or &quot;eruptions of bone-plate&quot;. Add in fangs, broken-bones-as-claws, bone-carapace shields. </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#0000FF\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">I don't have Abyssal Resistance charms </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">but I can do a hell-of-a-job emulating them!</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <b>Are these not all Lunar powers?</b> </div> </div> </div>Lunar Knacks from 2e are presumably all in limbo, and we're not getting shapeshifting into anything but beasts and humans, so presumably all of the expansions to the sacred hunt that go against this are going to be on the chopping block, which is, at this point, rather old news. Also, Abyssals aren't getting body horror in EX3, that's going to be Liminal territory.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193362#post1193362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bWell, there's no need to complain, because this is simply incorrect now. Eska of the Seven Blades' hybrid form barely looks bestial, and can easily be mistaken for something else. When she first showed up in the comic, people were uncertain if she even <i>was</i> a Lunar; I know I wouldn't have thought she was if she didn't turn into a bird at the end. That precedent is established, and it is perfectly valid for any future Lunars.<br /> <br /> \u200bHell, give Eska's mutations to something other than Extra Arms and keep the skin tone, and she'd look damn corpse-like herself.</div> </div> </div> </div>So what's the name of the Charm that builds on top of the base hybrid form and what do they call the totem of a Lunar, again?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T01:06:29-08:00","id":1193466,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23843_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23843\" data-vbnamecard=\"23843\">Salagimsim</a> to add an additional point about 3e being a significant shift on the lore front, the Devs are rolling back ALOT of 2nd ed world building to 1st ed. <a href=\"http://www.nishkriya.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.nishkriya.com/</a> has all the dev quotes from the MASSIVE Q&amp;A thread. If you\u2019re a setting junky it\u2019s well worth your time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas","name":"Saipjas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"270"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T04:01:53-08:00","id":1193485,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193463#post1193463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the name of the Charm that builds on top of the base hybrid form and what do they call the totem of a Lunar, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bSetting aside your attitude:<br /> <br /> \u200bDeadly Beastman Transformation's name does not matter; Vance has clarified that it need not involve any more physical change than looking physically stronger and more muscular, if even that. When Eska assumes it, she need not look any more spider-like than her hybrid shape normally does. After all, her write-up was based on the comic (right down to the detail of her previous weapons having been shattered), her write-up says that she always uses that Charm when she goes into combat, and in the comic, she retains the ashen-skinned, six-armed woman look even when fighting with intent to kill.<br /> <br /> \u200bSee also in the Ask the Devs thread, where Vance has said that mutations for Hybrid-Body Transformation include any mundane physical Merit, or how players get a lot of latitude in designing their hybrid forms.<br /> <br /> The idea that their hulked out form needs to obviously look animalistic is no longer correct.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T05:50:48-08:00","id":1193497,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11967-saipjas\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11967\" data-vbnamecard=\"11967\">Saipjas</a> <i>I was looking for something like this</i>. Thank you! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar158_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"158\" data-vbnamecard=\"158\">Isator Levi</a> <i>Thank you</i> for the 3E input. Still my blind-spot.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a> Let's be honest tho - it's disingenuous to &quot;shift the goal posts&quot; to reinforce your <i>very personal</i> preference (which no one is denying you). Ironically (?) this is precisely the approach I describe encountering in online games (where some other Lunar-fan disapproves of the 2nd, so they feel a need to preach their interpretation of <i>orthodoxy</i>).<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193463#post1193463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lunar Knacks from 2e are presumably all in limbo, and we're not getting shapeshifting into anything but beasts and humans, so presumably all of the expansions to the sacred hunt that go against this are going to be on the chopping block, which is, at this point, rather old news. Also, Abyssals aren't getting body horror in EX3, that's going to be Liminal territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>EX 3E is irrelevant when describing an EX 2E campaign (that was born and died years before 3E had a kickstarter). <b>The point is</b> that 2E had abundant <i>reinforcement and support</i> for &quot;Lunars as world-walkers&quot; who could masquerade as ghosts, demons, fae, etc. You can't deny what's in print. <i>Glories of Luna </i>even included NPCs such as converted-Fair Folk and a 3rd Circle Primordial <i>soul she wooed away - </i>Luna is not a <a href=\"https://youtu.be/hQZ6zzLpoNQ?t=7s\" target=\"_blank\">Disney Princess</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193463#post1193463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Non-native powers using hearthstones, artifacts, and sorcery/necromancy are just that - not effects that derive from the Charm set of a character type.</div> </div> </div> </div>So if I show you &quot;other Exalts blur the lines to masquerade as other things&quot;, you want native-powers.<br /> <br /> But if I show you native powers in 2E that are non-animalistic, you'll argue &quot;don't count on it for 3E!&quot;<br /> <br /> And if I include Exalts who masquerade <i>without even using powers</i>, you default to &quot;Stealth is OP&quot;.<br /> <br /> How do you feel about Infernals?<br /> <br /> A Fiend with Black Mirror Shintai <i>explicitly</i> copies someone down to charm-use.<br /> <br /> And what about the signature Slayer with the Blood Ape tote...coadjutor. Muscular neo-tribal covered in tattoos with ape-like arms and red hair, who hates the Realm (his people were slaughtered caught in a fight between them and the Bull of the North). If he uses BY RAGE RECAST, did the authors forget to include caveats on which mutations he's allowed? &quot;Oh sure, you can acquire horns - but they have to be made of brass and glow green!&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193463#post1193463\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what's the name of the Charm that builds on top of the base hybrid form and what do they call the totem of a Lunar, again?</div> </div> </div> </div>On top of DBT, it was always Perfected Hybrid Interaction - TBH, I can't recall taking DBT without PHI, because looking like a Ninja Turtle was never my thing.<br /> <br /> But we can quibble when they print the rules. <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4261/235096.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">Eska of the Seven Blades</a> is a <i>delight</i> (when I first saw her picture online, I thought it was a Fair Folk or Infernal - it was Isator who made me realize what she was).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T11:06:10-08:00","id":1193631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193485#post1193485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bSetting aside your attitude:</div> </div> </div> </div>If I am sour it is because long posts with alternating color font for emphasis targeted about Lunars reminds me of early 2012.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u200bDeadly Beastman Transformation's name does not matter; Vance has clarified that it need not involve any more physical change than looking physically stronger and more muscular, if even that. When Eska assumes it, she need not look any more spider-like than her hybrid shape normally does. After all, her write-up was based on the comic (right down to the detail of her previous weapons having been shattered), her write-up says that she always uses that Charm when she goes into combat, and in the comic, she retains the ashen-skinned, six-armed woman look even when fighting with intent to kill.<br /> <br /> \u200bSee also in the Ask the Devs thread, where Vance has said that mutations for Hybrid-Body Transformation include any mundane physical Merit, or how players get a lot of latitude in designing their hybrid forms.<br /> <br /> The idea that their hulked out form needs to obviously look animalistic is no longer correct. </div> </div> </div>What's your threshold on what counts as &quot;animalistic&quot; and what isn't? Because if all of the alterations are derived from their totem beast, they're still bestial shapeshifters even if they don't have faces that veer away from being mostly human. And in the end, too, Eska still turned into a bird and flew away. I don't see how it's not still animal-based shapeshifting all the way down, for all things concerning Lunar shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> (The totality of their Charm set is overwhelmingly likely to include things outside the realm of shapeshifting.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 03-09-2018, 02:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T12:51:48-08:00","id":1193676,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193631#post1193631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">long posts...alternating color font</div> </div> </div> </div>Deepest apologies - but when my &quot;Lunars can do this&quot; argument isn't seen as self-evident, quoting a dozen printed examples (that support my argument) is the rational follow-up. And the longer the post, the greater the need to break up walls of text - no?<br /> <br /> I do a mix of ad work and admin (mindmaps) - so making keywords <i>stand out</i> (for people who skim) is just a norm. I'm not claiming the results (on a forum) are <i>beautiful </i>- but it's way easier to articulate and edit thoughts. <i>I'm surprised</i> more people don't use them.<br /> <br /> Anyways, apologies - I'll try to curb the colors to a minimum.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193631#post1193631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your threshold on what counts as &quot;animalistic&quot; and what isn't? Because if all of the alterations are derived from their totem beast, they're still bestial shapeshifters even if they don't have faces that veer away from being mostly human. And in the end, too, Eska still turned into a bird and flew away. I don't see how it's not still animal-based shapeshifting all the way down, for all things concerning Lunar shapeshifting.<br /> <br /> (The totality of their Charm set is overwhelmingly likely to include things outside the realm of shapeshifting.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I just want to chime in that no one is <i>against animal-based shapeshifting</i>.<br /> <br /> But her arms &amp; face are her own. Human. She could be a recolored Hindi deity as much as anything (and if the description had not explicitly mentioned purple-and-silver wolf-spiders, <i>I would never have guessed</i>). I had seen the artwork online but overlooked it - <b>then</b> someone mentioned the artist and I thought it was a non-Exalted side-piece - <b>then</b> I was corrected, so I Thought she was a Fair Folk or Infernal in 3E. <b>Wolf-spiders</b> (by what I recall) are larger than web-spinning spiders (larger, hairier, chase prey instead of baiting them into traps). Eska isn't a bug-limbed, hairy, super-large spider-woman.<br /> <br /> I have <i>no complaints</i> about animalistic Lunars.<br /> <br /> I just <i>dislike</i> being told &quot;these allegedly amazing shapeshifters are <i>the most reliably predictable.&quot;</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Through indiscriminate suffering men know fear and fear is the most divine emotion.<br /> It is the stones for altars and the beginning of wisdom.<br /> Half gods are worshipped in wine and flowers. Real gods require blood.<br /> <b>- Their Eyes Were Watching God</b>","edited":{"userid":23843,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","user":"Salagimsim","date":".  typos 03-09-2018, 04:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23843-salagimsim","name":"Salagimsim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23843_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-09T15:01:07-08:00","id":1193714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193631#post1193631\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What's your threshold on what counts as &quot;animalistic&quot; and what isn't?</div> </div> </div> </div>In a spider totem? A lot more than four extra arms.<br /> <br /> \u200bMore eyes, more body hair, chelicerae, things that make them look a lot closer to spider.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because if all of the alterations are derived from their totem beast, they're still bestial shapeshifters even if they don't have faces that veer away from being mostly human.</div> </div> </div> </div>Are we talking about what they are, or what they look like? It seems to me that most of this conversation has been about cosmetics, not the underlying theme.<br /> <br /> \u200bGood Lord, Salagimsim went out of their way to cite all kinds of animals as the basis for getting some cadavariffic features, far more than even I, a significant advocate for animals in Lunars, would feel necessary, but that wasn't good enough for you.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">And in the end, too, Eska still turned into a bird and flew away. I don't see how it's not still animal-based shapeshifting all the way down, for all things concerning Lunar shapeshifting.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bAnd that would matter if anybody had asked for Lunars to turn into ghosts, rather than having mutations based on lizards to shoot blood out of their eyes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:22:27-08:00","id":1193897,"title":"","content":"Between Spirit Shapes being mechanically no different from any other animal form (at least for now) and the new expression of Hybrid Body Transformation, I'm now interested in playing or at least creating Lunars with totems I never would have considered before.<br /> <br /> For the classical choices of a cat or wolf totem, I'd like to play a swordsman who continues using his sword in Deadly Beastman Tranformation, only setting it aside for claws and fangs when using something like Terrifying Beastman Alteration or Devastating Ogre Enhance to go beyond &quot;Wolf-Eared Katana Guy&quot; into &quot;Hulking Werewolf Monster-Dude&quot;.<br /> <br /> I'd like to choose a grasshopper or beetle totem to be a Guyver or Kamen Rider; my Hybrid form would be my armored sentai henshin form. DBT would make me like <i>Bloody Roar's </i>Stun the Insect, and TBA/DOE would make me like Stun's monstrous super-form. With the extra mutations, I hope to afford both Wings and Subtlety for the wings, to hide them within the shell on my back.<br /> <br /> I could choose a bird of prey for a hawk-eyed archer.<br /> <br /> I could choose a turtle and be a reasonable approximation of a Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtle. Green-colored, Enhanced Smell, and with Unusual Hide to represent the leathery skin and armored shell (and possibly also the &quot;pull all extremities into shell&quot; trick). The ninja turtles really didn't have much else going for them in terms of obvious Supernatural Merits.<br /> <br /> <br /> One thing I do worry about<b></b>: Would it really be worth it for a Bear or Gorilla-totemed Lunar to ever fight as a bear or gorilla rather than using Deadly Beastman Transformation?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:32:59-08:00","id":1193900,"title":"","content":"Is there a mutation presently that makes you as good at brachiation as a gorilla?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T06:33:17-08:00","id":1193901,"title":"","content":"I've found that turning into a bear is pretty useful if you're a non-combat character. It's a cheap way to boost your rolls.<br /> <br /> But then, that's probably not the sort of character who has a Bear-totem.<br /> <br /> So, honestly... no, it's probably not as good as DBT, but saying this: DBT costs 8xp (plus 8 for Hybrid Body), and turning into your totem costs 0xp.<br /> <br /> Also, a gorilla-totem DBT would, in my mind, basically just be a massive gorilla, since they already are reasonably human-shaped.<br /> <br /> Also, there might be a couple of charms that are better in bear or gorilla form. We've already seen a couple of charms that give benefits in certain forms, I'm sure there's more, and it's likely a few of those apply to bear or gorilla form.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T10:19:30-08:00","id":1193967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193897#post1193897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I do worry about<b></b>: Would it really be worth it for a Bear or Gorilla-totemed Lunar to ever fight as a bear or gorilla rather than using Deadly Beastman Transformation?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI think yes. Eska, for example, can't get the extra benefit to Octopus and Spider Barrage unless she turns into her giant spider form, rather than her hybrid body. I'd lay even odds on there being quite a few Lunar Charms like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-10T21:35:22-08:00","id":1194134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193900#post1193900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a mutation presently that makes you as good at brachiation as a gorilla?</div> </div> </div> </div>There doesn't need to be. Gorillas aren't good at brachiation. They are very cautious tree climbers. <br /> <br /> They keep complaining about how their weight keeps bringing them down. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">\u200bNot that that should stop a Lunar Tarzan, but one would need a mutation that makes one as good at brachiation as <i>a gibbon</i>.</span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T01:05:48-08:00","id":1194173,"title":"","content":"I also remember there was some talk about how DBT might weaken your evocations. So, if you've got some badass moonsilver armour, you may well want to fight as a bear so you can be an armoured bear!<br /> <br /> (Assuming that's still the case).<br /> <br /> And one final thing... DBT is a good charm. But it's not an amazing charm, because while it gives you bonus damage and soak, it also gives you -1 Defence. That's a serious penalty. Bears don't get -1 Defence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T01:49:56-08:00","id":1194186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1194173#post1194173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And one final thing... DBT is a good charm. But it's not an amazing charm, because while it gives you bonus damage and soak, it also gives you -1 Defence. That's a serious penalty. Bears don't get -1 Defence.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, if the core is still correct, you will probably have an option to buy an upgrade that allows you to halve your wound penalties in DBT. Since from what we've seen so far, the Lunar Ox-Body mainly gives -2 and -4 health levels (-2/-4*3 at Stamina 4, to be specific), the defense penalty evens out after you've taken more than 3 levels of damage. Then, once you're in your -4s (which at Stamina 4 and just two purchases of OBT is half your health boxes), DBT is flat-out better for your defense, even if you ignore the rest of the bonuses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=943303#post943303\" target=\"_blank\">Evocations for the demonic tattoos gained from the Pact with Mara sorcerous initiation</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop?p=907071#post907071\" target=\"_blank\">Pyre-Kindler (Soulsteel and Red Jade Grimscythe, Artifact 3)</a> || <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1072019-soulsteel-stormcaller-concept-gravedigger?p=1074897#post1074897\" target=\"_blank\">Tenebrous Descent (Stormcaller's Black Jade Reaver Daiklave cousin, Artifact 5)</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1074256-combat-with-corebook-shikari-antagonists?p=1074303#post1074303\" target=\"_blank\">Advice for running the corebook shikari antagonists</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3443-aluminiumtrioxid","name":"aluminiumtrioxid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3443_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T03:21:08-07:00","id":1194195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1193897#post1193897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I do worry about<b></b>: Would it really be worth it for a Bear or Gorilla-totemed Lunar to ever fight as a bear or gorilla rather than using Deadly Beastman Transformation?</div> </div> </div> </div>Although Eska's write-up doesn't mention it, the core indicates that turning into an animal form grants a Lunar exalted the form's special attacks and merits. Well, the merits will probably be copied by the Hybrid Body Transformation, but Gorilla and Bear do get some nice special attacks. <br /> <br /> \u200bThere also may be circumstances when pretending to be merely a trained attack bear is preferable than being clearly an anathema.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T06:18:46-07:00","id":1194228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1194195#post1194195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although Eska's write-up doesn't mention it, the core indicates that turning into an animal form grants a Lunar exalted the form's special attacks and merits. <b>Well, the merits will probably be copied by the Hybrid Body Transformation</b>, but Gorilla and Bear do get some nice special attacks.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not so certain. A lot of special animal Merits are pretty powerful, and I don't expect to see them in PC hands outside of full-on shapeshifting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":97,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","user":"The MG","date":". 03-11-2018, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T07:33:44-07:00","id":1194241,"title":"","content":"Yeah, when it says Merits I'm pretty sure it's referring to the Merits in the Traits section, like wings, thick hide, etc, not the Merits in the animals section (for one thing, those don't have a points cost, so having X* points of merits to spend wouldn't allow you to buy any).<br /> <br /> *Anyone care to speculate on the number of points? Eska has 6 by my count. I did wonder if it's Stamina+Essence or Strength+Essence, but I suspect it's Essence +4, same as DBT used to give you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T10:23:15-07:00","id":1194288,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1194173#post1194173\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also remember there was some talk about how DBT might weaken your evocations.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bI dunno, I feel as though that's an element that wouldn't be coming with the new developers and how Arms finally elaborated on Evocations.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe whole question of it being related to how &quot;external&quot; an Exalt's powers were, well... a reference point in that discussion was Sidereals, and while it did technically still hold to the idea of Sidereals being the worst with Evocations, that still didn't leave them particularly limited with them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not complaining about that; in retrospect, I feel as though where Evocations were concerned, John kept wanting to add complications to them that they didn't really require, and that a severe limitation with them by Sidereals and war form Lunars was a part of that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it will be enough for there to be Charms that make use of your animal forms, which the hybrid form explicitly is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T11:09:21-07:00","id":1194303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1191798-sell-me-on-feeling-strongly-about-lunars?p=1194288#post1194288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bI dunno, I feel as though that's an element that wouldn't be coming with the new developers and how Arms finally elaborated on Evocations.<br /> <br /> \u200bThe whole question of it being related to how &quot;external&quot; an Exalt's powers were, well... a reference point in that discussion was Sidereals, and while it did technically still hold to the idea of Sidereals being the worst with Evocations, that still didn't leave them particularly limited with them.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not complaining about that; in retrospect, I feel as though where Evocations were concerned, John kept wanting to add complications to them that they didn't really require, and that a severe limitation with them by Sidereals and war form Lunars was a part of that.<br /> <br /> \u200bI think it will be enough for there to be Charms that make use of your animal forms, which the hybrid form explicitly is not.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1069023-ask-the-devs?p=1074156#post1074156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're thinking in the same direction I am. Ultimately it's going to depend on the balance needs of DBT, but I had some plans for it when I came up with Resonant/Dissonant.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems likely that DBT will lower resonance-&gt;normal, normal-&gt;dissonant, although that might change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-11T12:00:25-07:00","id":1194315,"title":"","content":"Don't just cite out-of-context quotes, say what was talked about! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">